      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Loads or retrieves a cached COF (Composite Object File) for a unit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate ppCofNodeList is non-NULL, assert if NULL\n2. Search existing node list for matching nUnitMode and nModeFlags\n3. If found, return pointer to cached COF data\n4. Build COF filename path using token type codes and mode codes\n5. Attempt to open file via SetAsyncFileHandle\n6. If file not found, return NULL\n7. Allocate UnitCofNode (8 bytes) and CofNode (0x20 bytes)\n8. Search global COF cache for matching entry, increment ref if found\n9. If not found, load COF data via Ordinal_10038/FUN_6f913fa2\n10. Verify COF header version is 0x14\n11. Link new nodes into lists and return COF data pointer\n\nParameters:\n- ppCofNodeList (void**): Pointer to head of unit-specific COF node list\n- dwTokenType (uint): Index into g_aszUnitTokenCodes (<=6=CHARS, >6=MONSTERS)\n- nUnitMode (int): Unit animation mode, stored at COF offset +4\n- dwWeaponCode (uint): Packed 4-byte weapon type code\n- dwArmorCode (uint): Packed 4-byte armor type code\n- nModeFlags (int): Mode-specific flags, stored at COF offset +0xC\n\nReturns:\n- byte*: Pointer to COF data at offset +0x14 of CofNode, or NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14: Required COF header version byte\n- 0x20 (32): Size of CofNode structure\n- 0x8: Size of UnitCofNode structure\n- 0x4B7: Assert line for NULL ppCofNodeList\n- 0x4C5: Assert line for UnitCofNode alloc\n- 0x4C6: Assert line for NULL UnitCofNode\n- 0x3DD: Assert line for NULL COF data\n- 0x3E6: Assert line for COF version mismatch\n- 0x4C9: Assert line for NULL CofNode\n- 0x4CF: Assert line for NULL COF data return",
