      "name": "CallFunctionOnArrayElements",
      "signature": "void CallFunctionOnArrayElements(void * pArrayBase, uint dwStride, int nCount, void * pfnCallback)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Iterates over array elements and calls a callback on each.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if nCount > 0 (count-1 >= 0)\n2. Loop nCount times, calling pfnCallback with element address in ECX\n3. Advance element pointer by dwStride each iteration\n\nParameters:\n- pArrayBase (void*): Start address of array (passed in ECX to callback)\n- dwStride (uint): Byte offset between elements\n- nCount (int): Number of elements to process\n- pfnCallback (void*): Function pointer called for each element\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nNotes:\n- Used to initialize arrays of objects (e.g., Unicode default constructors)\n- Callback receives element address via ECX register (__thiscall style)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
