      "name": "DrawChatUserTooltip",
      "signature": "int DrawChatUserTooltip(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Draws Battle.net chat user tooltip popup showing user type and account info.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate composite unit pointer via ECX (FogAssert if null)\n2. Initialize 256 Unicode string buffers for text lines\n3. Check if unit flags indicate tooltip should display (bit 3)\n4. Calculate tooltip rect based on unit X/Y position\n5. Determine user type from offset +0x1C and format title line:\n   - 0x10: Blizzard Rep\n   - 0x11: Moderator (also shows realm info)\n   - 0x12: Sysop\n   - 0x13: Referee\n   - 0x14: (unknown type)\n   - 0x15: Speaker\n   - 0x16: Open Character\n   - Otherwise: Game product type (Starcraft, Diablo, Warcraft II, etc.)\n6. Add realm info for D2DV/D2XP/D2ST products or Moderator\n7. Add \"Account Name: \" line with account string from offset +0xCC\n8. Calculate total tooltip width/height from string metrics\n9. Clamp X position to screen bounds (0-800)\n10. Draw each string line centered using Ordinal_10117\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: ECX contains CompositeUnit pointer\n\nReturns:\n- 0 if unit is null or flags don't allow tooltip\n- 1 on successful tooltip draw\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x208 (520): Stride for Unicode string array entries\n- 0x1E (30): Half-width offset for tooltip rect\n- 0x50 (80): Height offset for tooltip rect\n- 0x14 (20): Bottom padding for tooltip rect\n- 0x320 (800): Screen width boundary\n\nRelated Functions:\n- Ordinal_10170: Test if rect is visible\n- Ordinal_10127: Set text color/style\n- Ordinal_10131: Get string metrics (width/height)\n- Ordinal_10117: Draw Unicode string at position",
