      "name": "LoadItemExcelTables",
      "signature": "void LoadItemExcelTables(int nDataPtr)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Loads and initializes all item Excel data tables (weapons, armor, misc).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 180+ field descriptors on stack defining item txt column parsing rules\n2. Call LoadExcelTableData for weapons.txt, armor.txt, misc.txt\n3. Calculate combined item count and allocate unified buffer (DAT_6f924bbc)\n4. Copy all item records into combined buffer (weapons, armor, misc contiguous)\n5. Build sorted index array for items with levelreq=0\n6. Convert 3-char item codes to Unicode display names via GetStringIndex\n7. Build sorted lookup by item code via InsertSortedIndexEntry\n\nParameters:\n- nDataPtr (int): Pointer to data/file context passed to LoadExcelTableData\n\nReturns:\n- void (populates global item tables and indexes)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x250 (592): ItemRecord stride (bytes per item entry)\n- 0x94 (148): ItemRecord stride in DWORDs (0x250/4)\n- 0x80: Offset to 3-char item code in ItemRecord\n- 0xe8: Offset to Unicode item name buffer in ItemRecord\n- 0x40 (64): Max Unicode name length in chars\n- 0x16: Offset to levelreq field for index building\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- DAT_6f924bbc: Combined item table base pointer\n- DAT_6f924bd8: Sorted index array pointer\n- DAT_6f960900: Sorted code lookup table\n\nNote: ~600 local_* variables are compile-time field descriptor array elements,\nnot runtime variables. Each 20-byte descriptor defines column name, parse type,\ndefault value, struct offset, and flags for Excel txt parsing.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
