      "name": "InitItemTypesAndComponents",
      "signature": "void InitItemTypesAndComponents(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes item types and component type tables on first call.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check initialization flag (DAT_6f96094c) to prevent re-entry\n2. Load ItemTypes.bin via Ordinal_10038 and LoadItemTypesTable\n3. Zero g_adwComponentTypeTable array (0x2fd entries)\n4. Build field descriptor array for Excel table loader (equiv1/2, order, repair, identify, shoots, quiver, throwable, reload, reequip, autostack, magic, normal, charm, beltable, costformula, varinvgfx, invgfx1-5)\n5. Load itemtypes table via LoadExcelTableData -> g_pItemTypesTable\n6. Load hitclass table via LoadExcelTableData\n7. Call LoadItemExcelTables for additional item data\n8. For each item in g_pItemTable:\n   - Get component code from offset 0x84 or 0x80\n   - Check if item type is armor/weapon via IsItemTypeEquivalent (types 0x2D, 3, 2, 0x25, 0x4B)\n   - Find or create entry in g_adwComponentTypeTable\n   - Store item type byte (offset 0x26) in g_adwComponentFrameTable\n   - Lookup animation frame index from g_pItemTable+0x8C mapping\n9. Set g_nComponentTypeCount to 0xFF\n\nParameters:\n- None (void function)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2fd (765): Component type table size\n- 0x250 (592): Item record stride\n- 0x84/0x80: Component code offsets in item record\n- 0x26: Item type byte offset\n- 0x8C: Animation mapping offset\n- 0x2D (45): Armor type\n- 0x32 (50): Shield type\n- 0x4B (75): Jewel type",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:28fc17bb1654ac53c62764435708deaa",
