      "name": "InitializeTransformTables",
      "signature": "void InitializeTransformTables(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes two transformation lookup tables by applying a transform function to triplets of input bytes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through first input table (g_abTransformTable1Data) in strides of 3\n2. Call Ordinal_10034 with each triplet (previous, current, next bytes)\n3. Store result byte in output table (g_abTransformTable1Out)\n4. Repeat for second input table (g_abTransformTable2Data) to output (g_abTransformTable2Out)\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: ESI, EDI used for loop control\n- Input tables: g_abTransformTable1Data, g_abTransformTable2Data\n- Output tables: g_abTransformTable1Out, g_abTransformTable2Out\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3: Triplet stride (3-byte groups)\n- Table boundaries: 0x6f91f1a7, 0x6f91f1c7 (loop termination addresses)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:f99b8bde9109e0e16b02449aa1ab04a0",
