      "name": "CreateUnit",
      "signature": "void * CreateUnit(dword nUnitType, dword nSubType, dword nX, dword nY, dword nGfxType, dword * pdwInitData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a unit object with specified attributes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x58 (88) bytes of memory for unit structure\n2. Clear all fields to zero\n3. Set type field (offset 0) to 0xc\n4. Apply type and state bit masks to field at offset 2\n5. Store parameters into structure fields (type, subtype, coordinates, gfx type)\n6. Set function pointers for event handlers\n7. Copy initialization data from pdwInitData or use defaults\n8. Invoke post-initialization handler (FUN_6f90ea50)\n9. Return allocated unit pointer\n\nParameters:\n- nUnitType (ECX): Unit type identifier (stored at offset 0xc)\n- nSubType (EDX): Unit subtype/class (stored at offset 0x14)\n- nX (Stack+0x4): X coordinate (stored at offset 0x18)\n- nY (Stack+0x8): Y coordinate (stored at offset 0x1c)\n- nGfxType (Stack+0xc): Graphics type flag (stored at offset 0x4c)\n- pdwInitData (Stack+0x10): Optional pointer to 2-dword initialization data\n\nReturns:\n- void*: Pointer to newly allocated and initialized unit structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:45ebb3d7098adc3d1cf0a485b4cc2cf8",
