      "name": "AccountInsertName",
      "signature": "void AccountInsertName(int * pAccount, char * szName)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Inserts an account name record into a linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate account has expected type 0xc, assert on mismatch\n2. Allocate 0x38 (56) bytes for account name node\n3. Copy up to 0x32 (50) bytes from input string to node\n4. Clear bytes 0x34-0x37 with null terminators\n5. Link into account list at offset 0x40 (FIFO - new node points to old head, becomes new head)\n\nParameters:\n- pAccount (int*): Pointer to account structure; offset 0x0 contains type field, offset 0x40 contains name list head\n- szName (char*): Input string to copy (max 0x32 bytes, null-terminated not required)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xc (12): Account structure type identifier\n- 0x38 (56): Size of allocated name node\n- 0x32 (50): Maximum name string length\n- 0x34-0x37: Null terminator quad-word in name node\n- 0x40 (64): Offset of name list head in account structure\n\nStructure Layout:\nName node [0x38 bytes]:\n- [0x0:0x33] (52 bytes): Name string buffer\n- [0x34:0x37] (4 bytes): Next pointer (linked list)",
