      "name": "CreateUIElementType6",
      "signature": "void * CreateUIElementType6(dword nClassId, dword nElementId, int nWidth, int nHeight, dword dwFlags, dword dwParam1, int nEventHandler, dword dwParam2, dword byFlags, int nStringId, dword dwParam3)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Factory function that creates and initializes a UI element structure of type 6.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x274 bytes (157 dwords) for UI element structure\n2. Zero-initialize the entire structure with REP STOSD\n3. Set base type field to 6 and apply bitmasked flags\n4. Initialize element and class IDs, dimensions\n5. Setup event handler function pointer (if provided)\n6. Apply additional flags and parameters to structure fields\n7. Validate and copy string resource if ID provided\n8. Calculate tile dimensions from width/height with 256-unit scaling\n9. Conditionally double tile count if flag 0x20 is set\n10. Call initialization function FUN_6f90ea50\n\nParameters:\n- nClassId (dword in ECX): Class/type identifier\n- nElementId (dword in EDX): Element instance ID\n- nWidth (int): Element width in units\n- nHeight (int): Element height in units\n- dwFlags (dword): Initialization flags\n- dwParam1 (dword): Supplementary parameter\n- nEventHandler (int): Event handler code (0=none)\n- dwParam2 (dword): Additional parameter for handler\n- byFlags (dword): Control flags with bit 0x20 for tile doubling\n- nStringId (int): String resource ID to copy\n- dwParam3 (dword): Final parameter\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to newly allocated and initialized UI element structure (620 bytes)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:db2fd009d675e4a43e8dc892e8c9493f",
