      "name": "SetButtonField",
      "signature": "void SetButtonField(int * pBtn, int nValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Assigns a value to a button structure field at a fixed offset.\n\nValidates the button structure type and sets field at offset 0x270 to the\nprovided value. Terminates execution if structure type validation fails.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if structure type field (offset 0) equals 6\n2. If type mismatch, call FogAssert with error details and abort\n3. Write nValue to button field at offset 0x270 (0x9c * 4 bytes)\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pBtn (int*): Button/window structure pointer (ECX in __fastcall)\n- nValue (int): Value to store in button field at offset 0x270\n\nReturns:\n- void: Function never returns on type validation failure (calls abort)\n- void: Normal return after successful field assignment\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 6: Expected button structure type indicator\n- 0x270: Field offset in button structure (588 bytes, or 0x9c dwords)\n- 0x100: Assertion line number (256)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:5961bc025d7a777652eba205bcb177b7",
