      "name": "FireButtonCallback",
      "signature": "uint FireButtonCallback(int * pButton)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Fires button callback if conditions are met.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate button type is 6 (assert if not)\n2. Set button state bits using gdwBitMasks\n3. Check if button should fire based on state and mask flags\n4. If conditions met and callback exists, invoke callback with button pointer\n5. Clear fired state flag\n6. Return callback result or 0\n\nParameters:\n- pButton (int*): Pointer to button structure\n\nReturns:\n- Result from button callback, or 0 if callback not invoked\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 6: Expected button type value\n- 0x10, 0x11, 0x12, 0xd: Button structure offsets\n- gdwBitMasks_exref: Global bit mask table",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
