      "name": "EditBoxProcessClipboardInput",
      "signature": "int EditBoxProcessClipboardInput(void * pEditData, Unicode nCharMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Processes clipboard text input for edit control with character encoding conversion.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validates input parameter (ptEditData) and character mode (nCharMode)\n2. Checks enabled state via flags (0x20, 0x8, 0x10, 0x4)\n3. Handles callback invocation if mode is 0x9 and callback flag set\n4. Validates character via Ordinal_10128 (character validity check)\n5. Swaps selection if selection exists and mode not 0x1, 0x3, 0x18\n6. Processes specific character modes: 0x1 (select all), 0xd/0xe (newline), 0x3 (copy), 0x16 (paste), 0x18 (delete)\n7. For paste (0x16): Retrieves clipboard, filters CR/LF if mode bit 0x8 unset, concatenates text\n8. For draw mode (bit 0x8): Calculates text rendering dimensions with line wrapping\n9. Updates edit control text buffer and cursor position\n10. Invokes change callback if set\n\nParameters:\n- pEditData (void*): Pointer to ptEditData control structure (offset-based field access)\n- nCharMode (Unicode): Character mode/command (0x1=select-all, 0x3=copy, 0x16=paste, 0x18=delete, 0xd/0xe=newline)\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on failure or early exit (validation failed, callback returned 0, no clipboard)\n- 1 on success (after processing mode and updating edit control)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x268: Offset to callback function pointer in ptEditData\n- 0x25c: Offset to character position (cursor) in ptEditData\n- 0x54/0x58: Selection start/end positions in ptEditData\n- 0x260: Offset to mode flags (0x20=enable input, 0x8=wrap-render, 0x10=special flag, 0x4=callback flag)\n- 0x5c: Offset to text buffer pointer in ptEditData\n- 0x48: Maximum text length in ptEditData\n- 0x44/0x40/0x14/0x18: Layout dimensions for text rendering\n- 0x6f960b90: Global clipboard memory handle\n- 0x6f960988: Global paste buffer (0x200 bytes)",
