      "name": "EditData_SetString",
      "signature": "int EditData_SetString(EditData * pEditData, Unicode * pwszValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Sets a Unicode string value in an EditData structure with validation and callback.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pEditData pointer is non-null and type field equals 1\n2. Obtain string length via Unicode::strlen(pwszValue)\n3. If length is 0, zero out the string buffer at offset 0x17\n4. If length > 0, copy pwszValue to offset 0x17 via Unicode::strcpy()\n5. Store string length at offset 0x97\n6. Invoke post-processing function FUN_6f90b4a0 (likely updates display)\n7. Check for callback at offset 0x9b and invoke if present (with param 0)\n8. Return 1 on success\n\nParameters:\n- pEditData (EditData*): Pointer to EditData structure (must be non-null, type=1)\n- pwszValue (Unicode*): New Unicode string value to set in EditData\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success\n- Does not return if validation fails (calls FUN_6f91436d to abort)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:f37eae4b9486cb4175333f44901ab791",
