      "name": "RenderEditBoxControl",
      "signature": "void RenderEditBoxControl(int * pEditData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Render callback for edit box UI controls. Draws text content with cursor and selection highlighting.\n\nSource: D2WinEditBox.cpp\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - invoked as render function pointer from UI element structure\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate pEditData pointer and type field (must be D2WIN_EDITBOX = 1)\n2. Check visibility flags via gdwBitMasks_exref bits 0 and 8\n3. If not in game state, clear active selection state (offset 0xa0)\n4. If selection active, send WM_LBUTTONDOWN message to ProcessEditBoxMessage\n5. Initialize 600-byte Unicode display buffer (300 wchars)\n6. If flags field set, clear EditData structure and call GfxInterfaceCall84 for background\n7. Set active font from pEditData[0x9c]\n8. Calculate render position: X = offset 0x10 + offset 0x03, Y = (0x11 - 0x06) + 16 + offset 0x04\n9. Copy visible text substring from pEditData text buffer (offsets 0x13 to 0x14) to display buffer\n10. If password mask flag (offset 0x98 bit 0) set, replace text with g_wLineSeparator characters\n11. Validate type field again (assertion)\n12. If no selection or collapsed selection (0x15 == -1 or 0x15 == 0x16):\n    - Render full text with RenderUnicodeTextWithLineHeight using color from offset 0x9d\n13. Else (active selection):\n    - Find selection color via FindPaletteIndexForColor(0x40, 0x40, 0x40) for gray\n    - Split text into 3 parts: before selection, selected text, after selection\n    - Calculate pixel positions for each segment via GetUnicodeStringDimensions\n    - Render pre-selection text normally\n    - Render selected text with RenderTextWithShadow (highlighted)\n    - Render post-selection text normally\n14. Check if this control has input focus via GetLastInputTime\n15. If focused and cursor blink phase active (GetTickCount / 250 is odd):\n    - Calculate cursor X position via CalcStringCharWidthSum\n    - Render cursor character (g_wLineEndMarker) at cursor position\n16. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pEditData (int*, ECX via __fastcall): Pointer to edit box control structure (0x284 bytes)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success\n\nEdit Box Structure Layout (offsets as dword indices):\nOffset | Field | Description\n0x00   | eType | Control type (1 = D2WIN_EDITBOX)\n0x01   | dwFlags | State flags\n0x02   | dwVisibility | Visibility bitmask (checked against gdwBitMasks_exref)\n0x03   | nX | X position\n0x04   | nY | Y position\n0x06   | nWidth | Control width\n0x10   | nXOffset | X render offset\n0x11   | nYOffset | Y render offset\n0x13   | nVisibleStart | First visible character index\n0x14   | nVisibleEnd | Last visible character index\n0x15   | nSelStart | Selection start (-1 if none)\n0x16   | nSelEnd | Selection end\n0x17   | wszText | Unicode text buffer (at byte offset 0x5c)\n0x97   | nCursorPos | Cursor character position\n0x98   | dwExFlags | Extended flags (bit 0 = password mask)\n0x9c   | nFontId | Active font identifier\n0x9d   | dwTextColor | Text color value\n0xa0   | dwActiveState | Active/dragging state\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xfa (250): Cursor blink period divisor in milliseconds\n- 0x40, 0x40, 0x40: Selection highlight color (gray RGB)\n- 0x5c (92): Byte offset to text buffer within structure\n- 300: Display buffer size in Unicode characters\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ProcessEditBoxMessage: Handles input events for this control\n- CreateUIElementType1: Creates edit box and assigns this as render callback\n- EditBoxHandleSelectionWrapper: Alternative handler for extended flags bit 3",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:f31912f0712f95df06caed06c1135a6c",
