      "name": "EditBoxHandleSelectionWrapper",
      "signature": "void EditBoxHandleSelectionWrapper(dword * pEditBox)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Wrapper for EditBoxHandleSelection with screen-relative coordinate calculation.\n\nClassification: Thunk/Wrapper - translates screen coordinates to edit box local coordinates\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Dereference pEditBox to get edit data pointer (pnEditData)\n2. Assert pnEditData is non-NULL\n3. Assert edit data type field equals 1 (EDITBOX type)\n4. Calculate Y coordinate: g_nScreenHeight - pnEditData[0x10] - pnEditData[3]\n   (screen height minus line height minus Y position)\n5. Calculate X coordinate: pnEditData[6] - pnEditData[0x11] - pnEditData[4] + g_nScreenWidth\n   (width minus left margin minus X position plus screen width)\n6. Call EditBoxHandleSelection(pEditBox, nStartX, nStartY)\n\nParameters:\n- pEditBox (dword *): Pointer to edit box wrapper containing edit data pointer at offset 0\n\nReturns:\n- void (no return value)\n\nStructure Offsets (pnEditData array):\n- [0x00]: eType - element type (1 = EDITBOX)\n- [0x03]: nX - X position\n- [0x04]: nY - Y position\n- [0x06]: nWidth - total width\n- [0x10]: nLineHeight - text line height\n- [0x11]: nLeftMargin - left margin offset\n\nRelated Functions:\n- EditBoxHandleSelection: Main selection handler this wrapper calls\n- ProcessEditBoxMessage: Alternative message handler (non-wrapper version)\n- CreateUIElementType1: Creates edit boxes, stores this function at pObject[9]\n\nUsage Context:\nStored as callback at pObject[9] when CreateUIElementType1 is called with dwExFlags bit 3 set.\nProvides simplified coordinate transformation compared to ProcessEditBoxMessage.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:f37eae4b9486cb4175333f44901ab791",
