      "name": "IsCharDigit",
      "signature": "int IsCharDigit(int nUnused1, int nUnused2, char * szChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Checks if a character is a decimal digit (0-9).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load character from szChar pointer\n2. Compare with ASCII '0' (0x30)\n3. If less than '0', return 0\n4. Compare with ASCII '9' (0x39)\n5. If greater than '9', return 0\n6. Return 1 if within range\n\nParameters:\n- nUnused1 (int): Unused, passed for API compatibility\n- nUnused2 (int): Unused, passed for API compatibility\n- szChar (char*): Pointer to character to test\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if character is digit (0-9), 0 otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x30 (48): ASCII '0'\n- 0x39 (57): ASCII '9'",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:43089d2dcbc2a56f9a983b729d68491c",
