      "name": "EditBoxValidateInsert",
      "signature": "void EditBoxValidateInsert(int nEditBoxPtr)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Validates and adjusts cursor position for inserting text into edit box while respecting width constraints.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate available width by subtracting used bytes from maximum allowed width\n2. Convert input string to Unicode (if in binary mode) or copy directly\n3. Measure width of converted/copied string and line ending\n4. Determine if text fits without overflow\n5. If fits, clear selection and set end position\n6. If text overflow occurs, adjust cursor position via binary search:\n   - When expanding selection: move backward from current position while text width < available\n   - When shrinking selection: move forward from current position while text width < available\n   - When within selection: search from current position toward limits\n\nParameters:\n- pEditBox (ECX): Pointer to EditBoxData structure containing buffer, positions, and constraints\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5c: Offset of string buffer in EditBoxData\n- 0x25c: Offset of selection end in EditBoxData\n- 0x260: Offset of edit mode flags (bit 0 = binary mode)\n- 300: Initial Unicode string capacity on stack\n- 0x270: Offset for cleanup call\n\nRelated: EditData_SetString, ProcessEditBoxMessage, EditBoxKeyHandler",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:e920968c4fe99771a55cdecfba1be3fd",
