      "name": "InitStringBufferUnicode",
      "signature": "void InitStringBufferUnicode(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Initializes the global Unicode string buffer with 1024 elements.\n\nClassification: Initialization function\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Set ESI to point to g_pszStringBuffer (0x6F960CC8)\n2. Set loop counter EDI to 0x400 (1024)\n3. Loop: Call Unicode::_default_constructor_closure_ via [0x6F91D05C]\n4. Increment ESI by 2 (sizeof wchar_t)\n5. Decrement EDI and loop until zero\n6. Restore registers and return\n\nParameters: None\n\nReturns: void\n\nMemory Model:\n- Modifies: g_pszStringBuffer (2048 bytes = 1024 wide chars)\n- Preserves: ESI, EDI (saved/restored)\n\nRelated Globals:\n- g_pszStringBuffer @ 0x6F960CC8: Unicode buffer being initialized\n- PTR_default_constructor_closure @ 0x6F91D05C: Unicode element initializer\n\nNotes:\n- Function has incomplete boundaries in Ghidra (shows 1-byte body)\n- Actual code spans 0x6f90b700 to 0x6f90b71c (29 bytes)\n- Pattern: PUSH ESI/EDI, loop with indirect call, POP EDI/ESI, RET\n\nRaw Assembly (manual disassembly):\n  6f90b700: PUSH ESI\n  6f90b701: PUSH EDI\n  6f90b702: MOV ESI, 0x6F960CC8\n  6f90b707: MOV EDI, 0x400\n  6f90b70c: MOV ECX, ESI\n  6f90b70e: CALL [0x6F91D05C]\n  6f90b714: ADD ESI, 2\n  6f90b717: DEC EDI\n  6f90b718: JNZ 0x6f90b70c\n  6f90b71a: POP EDI\n  6f90b71b: POP ESI\n  6f90b71c: RET",
