      "name": "InitializeAnimationCodeStrings",
      "signature": "void InitializeAnimationCodeStrings(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Initializes the global Unicode animation code string array.\n\nCalled during D2Win initialization to set up two Unicode string objects\nat g_wsAnimationCode (0x6f9614dc) for animation sequence codes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pointer to g_wsAnimationCode global array\n2. Set loop counter to 2 (two Unicode objects to initialize)\n3. For each iteration:\n   a. Call Unicode::_default_constructor_closure_ on current object\n   b. Advance pointer by 2 bytes to next Unicode object\n   c. Decrement counter\n4. Loop until counter reaches 0\n5. Return\n\nParameters:\nNone - void function\n\nReturns:\nvoid - No return value\n\nClassification: Initialization function - sets up Unicode string state\n\nMemory Model:\n- Modifies: g_wsAnimationCode[2] - two Unicode objects initialized\n- No allocations - operates on pre-allocated global storage\n- Called once during module initialization\n\nCross-References:\n- Referenced from 0x6f91f00c (initialization table)\n- g_wsAnimationCode used by: GetStringDisplayWidth, CalcUnicodeStringWidth,\n  InitializeLocaleFontResources, RenderCelShadedText\n\nNote: Function boundaries in Ghidra show only PUSH ESI due to analysis issue.\nActual function is ~29 bytes ending with RET at 0x6f90b75c.",
