      "name": "ReleaseFontHeapResources",
      "signature": "void ReleaseFontHeapResources(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Releases all cached CelFile and pool allocation resources.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load pointer to resource entry array from g_pFontHeap\n2. Test CelFile handle at current offset minus 4 bytes (previous entry field)\n3. Call ReleaseCelFile if handle is non-NULL to release CelFile resources\n4. Clear the released CelFile handle to NULL\n5. Test pool allocation handle at current offset\n6. Call ReleasePoolAllocation if handle is non-NULL with size parameter 0x134\n7. Clear the released pool allocation handle to NULL\n8. Increment pointer by stride of 0x14 bytes (5 dwords) to next entry\n9. Compare pointer against boundary address 0x6f960cb4\n10. Loop back to step 2 until all entries processed\n11. Load and release the master CelFile handle from g_dwDefaultCelIndex\n12. Clear master CelFile handle to NULL\n\nParameters:\n  IMPLICIT g_pFontHeap: Global array of resource entries to be released\n  IMPLICIT g_dwDefaultCelIndex: Global master CelFile handle to be released\n\nReturns:\n  void: Function returns with no value\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Entry array uses stride of 0x14 (20) bytes = 5 dwords per entry\n  - CelFile handle stored at offset -4 from current position (previous field)\n  - Pool allocation size hardcoded as 0x134 (308) bytes\n  - Array boundary check at address 0x6f960cb4 determines iteration count",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:1572c0263df9e4ec31d4d6828700cef3",
