      "name": "RenderCelShadedText",
      "signature": "void RenderCelShadedText(Unicode * pszString, uint nX, int nY, undefined4 nMinVal, int nMaxVal, int param_6)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Renders text with cel-shaded character animations, parsing escape codes.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate nMaxVal >= 0 (max pixel count)\n2. Initialize CEL file cache (aCStack_48) to zero\n3. Iterate through Unicode string characters\n4. On 0xFF escape: identify code type (color 'a'/'b' or animation 'v')\n5. On LF (0x0A): apply line height, advance Y position\n6. For normal glyphs: lookup CEL data, validate width bounds\n7. Render via Ordinal_10074, advance X position\n\nParameters:\n- pszString (Unicode*): Unicode string with embedded escape codes\n- nX (int): X starting position in pixels\n- nY (int): Y starting position in pixels\n- nMinVal (int): Minimum allowed pixel width\n- nMaxVal (int): Maximum allowed pixel width (-1 = unlimited)\n\nReturns:\n- void",
