      "signature": "int GetStringDisplayWidth(ushort * pwszText)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Calculate the maximum display width of a Unicode string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input string is not null\n2. Get string length via Unicode::strlen()\n3. Loop through each character in the string\n4. For line feed (0x0A), update max width if current exceeds it, reset current width\n5. For non-ASCII characters (>0xFF) or animation codes, call g_pfnValueProcessor to get character width\n6. Accumulate character widths into current line width\n7. Update maximum width at loop end\n\nParameters:\n- pwszText (wchar_t*): Unicode string to measure; cannot be null\n\nReturns:\n- Maximum display width in pixels of the text string",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
