      "name": "RenderUnicodeStringWithColors",
      "signature": "void RenderUnicodeStringWithColors(Unicode * pszText, int nX, int nY, int nWidth, int nColorIndex, int nCentered)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Renders Unicode text with embedded color codes at specified screen location.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate text length and initial X position (handle centering if requested)\n2. Initialize CEL_DATA structure (18 dwords) for sprite rendering\n3. Set current color from global font table: g_pdwCelDataTable\n4. Main loop - iterate through text characters:\n   - If 0xFF escape: Parse color code (next char - 0x30), validate range [0,12]\n   - If 0x0A newline: Reset X to column start, advance Y by line height\n   - Otherwise: Render character via Ordinal_10073, advance X by char width\n5. Exit when cursor exceeds text length\n\nParameters:\n- pszText (Unicode*): Pointer to Unicode string (UTF-16LE encoded)\n- nX (int): Initial X coordinate for rendering\n- nY (int): Y coordinate (modified by newlines)\n- nWidth (int): Available width for centering calculation\n- nColorIndex (int): Default color index (0-12)\n- nCentered (int): If non-zero, center text horizontally\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xFF: Color escape prefix character\n- 0x30: ASCII '0', subtracted from next char to get index\n- 0x0C: Color range limit (13 colors, indices 0-12)\n- 0x12: CEL_DATA structure size (18 dwords)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:96198456aba9787ea7af1e47e358e62f",
