      "name": "RenderMultilineUnicodeText",
      "signature": "void RenderMultilineUnicodeText(Unicode * pszText, int nX, int nY, dword dwColor)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Renders multi-line Unicode text with color styling at specified position.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate text pointer is non-null (assert if invalid)\n2. Count newlines (0x000a) in Unicode string to determine total line count\n3. Fetch current font height from g_pFontHandles using g_nCurrentFontIndex\n4. Calculate total text height: (font_height * g_dwHeightScale * line_count) / 10\n5. Adjust nX coordinate to fit within ESI-retaddr bounds\n6. Adjust nY coordinate to fit within EBX-0x1f bounds\n7. Reserve top margin and adjust rendering Y if needed\n8. Call Ordinal_10055 to clear/prepare rendering area with background\n9. Call RenderUnicodeStringWithColors to render text with dwColor style\n\nParameters:\n- pszText (Unicode*): Null-terminated Unicode string; may contain newlines (0x000a)\n- nX (int): Target X coordinate for text position\n- nY (int): Target Y coordinate for text position  \n- dwColor (dword): Color/style flags passed to RenderUnicodeStringWithColors\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14 (20): Font handle array element stride\n- 10 (0xa): Height/width scaling divisor\n- 0x1f (31): Width boundary offset constant\n- 2: Multiline text margin adjustment factor",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:8ce179ae006b7fcf242898828f000990",
