      "name": "CreateUIElementType2",
      "signature": "void * CreateUIElementType2(dword dwParam1, dword dwParam2, dword dwParam4, dword dwParam5, dword dwFlags, dword dwParam8, dword dwParam9, dword dwParam10)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Creates a Type 2 UI element with initialized structure fields.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x4c (76) bytes for UI element structure via FogMemAlloc\n2. Initialize all dwords to 0 using REP STOSD loop\n3. Set type field to 2 and apply bit masks from gdwBitMasks_exref\n4. Copy parameters into structure fields at offsets [1], [3], [4], [5], [6], [8], [9], [10], [0xc], [0xd], [0x12]\n5. Set function pointers and callback addresses at offsets [7], [9]\n6. Call FUN_6f90ea50 to finalize initialization\n7. Return pointer to initialized structure\n\nParameters:\n- dwParam1 (ECX): Stored at structure offset [3]\n- dwParam2 (EDX): Stored at structure offset [4]\n- dwParam4: Stored at structure offset [5]\n- dwParam5: Stored at structure offset [6]\n- dwFlags: Stored at structure offset [1], combined with bit masks\n- dwParam8: Stored at structure offset [8]\n- dwParam9: Stored at structure offset [9]\n- dwParam10: Stored at structure offset [0xc]\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated and initialized UI element structure (never NULL)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x4c (76): Total structure size in bytes\n- 0x13 (19): Number of dwords to zero-initialize\n- 2: Type identifier for this UI element class\n- Offsets [0]-[0x12]: Structure field indices",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
