      "name": "DrawSpriteFrame",
      "signature": "dword DrawSpriteFrame(int * pSpriteData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Draws a sprite frame with clipping and tiling to the render buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate image type (must be type 2)\n2. Check bit masks against sprite flags\n3. Initialize local frame buffer and iterate through rows\n4. For each row, tile column-wise, calling drawing function per tile\n5. Handle partial rows/columns with edge clipping\n6. Return 1 on success, 0 on flag mismatch\n\nParameters:\n- pSpriteData (int *): Pointer to sprite data array containing:\n  [0] = image type (must be 2)\n  [1] = optional context/mode\n  [2] = flag bits for validation\n  [3] = Y position (base)\n  [4] = X position (base)\n  [5] = height in pixels\n  [6] = width in pixels\n  [0x10] = frame index\n  [0x11] = palette/color mode\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if flags valid and drawing completed\n- 0 if flags do not match validation masks\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xff: Pixel/tile boundary mask\n- 0x100: Tile size (256 pixels)\n- 0x101: Adjustment constant for clipping\n- 18: Frame buffer array size",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
