      "name": "GetListElementAtIndex",
      "signature": "int GetListElementAtIndex(int * pList, int nIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Returns the node pointer at the specified index in a linked list.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert that pList points to a valid list structure (*pList == 7)\n2. Load the list head pointer from pList[0x19]\n3. Loop through nIndex nodes by dereferencing offset 0x220 (next pointer)\n4. Return the node pointer at that index, or 0 if list is empty or index exceeds length\n\nParameters:\n- pList (int*): Pointer to list control structure, head stored at offset 0x19\n- nIndex (int): Zero-based index of desired list element to retrieve\n\nReturns:\n- int: Pointer to the list node at the specified index, or 0 if not found\n\nNotes:\n- Each list node has a next pointer at offset 0x220\n- Type field (*pList) must equal 7 for linked list type",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
