      "name": "RenderTextListWidget",
      "signature": "int RenderTextListWidget(int * pWidget)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Render callback for text list widget - draws list items with optional selection markers.\n\nNOTE: Function boundaries are broken in Ghidra (only 1 instruction in body).\n      Run RecreateFunction_6f90e110.java via Script Manager to fix.\n      Variables below are from decompiler flow analysis, not formal Ghidra locals.\n\nClassification: Callback/Handler - Widget render callback invoked by UI system\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate widget type is 7 (text list), assert if not\n2. Set active font from widget font index (offset 0x40)\n3. Calculate initial Y position from widget geometry\n4. Skip N entries based on scroll position (offset 0x4C)\n5. Zero-initialize 18-dword render state array on stack\n6. Set pentagram image reference from g_pPentagramImage\n7. Loop through visible list items:\n   a. If item is selected (matches offset 0x68), render pentagram markers\n      - Left marker at (x - width/4 - 25, y + 3 or y + 9)\n      - Right marker at (x + width - width/4 - 25, y + 3 or y + 9)\n   b. Render item text centered horizontally\n   c. Store item bounding box at offsets 0x208-0x214\n   d. Advance to next item via linked list (offset 0x220)\n   e. Advance Y by line height + spacing\n8. Increment animation frame counter (offset 0x5C), wrap at 8\n9. Restore font to default (1)\n10. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pWidget (int * via ECX): Pointer to text list widget structure (0x6C bytes)\n\nLocal Variables (from decompiler analysis):\n- iVar1 (int): Text width from pszText+0x200\n- iVar2 (int): Widget X position (pWidget[3])\n- iVar3 (int): Loop counter / widget width / temp\n- iVar4 (int): Selection marker X offset calculation\n- piVar5 (int *): Stack array initialization pointer\n- pszText (Unicode *): Current text item pointer\n- nY (int): Current Y rendering position\n- uStack_50 (uint): Selection marker Y position (y+3 or y+9)\n- aiStack_48 (int[18]): GfxInterfaceCall84 render state array\n\nWidget Structure Offsets:\n- 0x00: Type (must be 7)\n- 0x0C: X position (pWidget[3])\n- 0x10: Y position (pWidget[4])\n- 0x14: Width (pWidget[5])\n- 0x18: Height (pWidget[6])\n- 0x40: Font index (pWidget[0x10])\n- 0x44: Line height (pWidget[0x11])\n- 0x48: Line spacing (pWidget[0x12])\n- 0x4C: Scroll position (pWidget[0x13])\n- 0x5C: Animation frame 0-7 (pWidget[0x17])\n- 0x60: Max text width (pWidget[0x18])\n- 0x64: Text list head (pWidget[0x19])\n- 0x68: Selected item (pWidget[0x1a])\n\nText Item Structure Offsets (0x224 bytes):\n- 0x000-0x1FF: Unicode text content (255 chars max)\n- 0x200: Text width in pixels\n- 0x208: Bounding box left\n- 0x20C: Bounding box right\n- 0x210: Bounding box top\n- 0x214: Bounding box bottom\n- 0x220: Next item pointer (linked list)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Always returns success (after valid type check)\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n- g_pPentagramImage (0x6f9614f4): Selection marker image handle\n\nCalled From:\n- CreateTextListWidget: Stored at pWidget[7] as render callback\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Font index 2 uses y+9 offset for selection markers, others use y+3\n- Animation frame wraps from 7 to 0 each render call",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:71fbe7a641b86d022a20f0d2e2db16a7",
