      "name": "HandleTextListEvent",
      "signature": "int HandleTextListEvent(int * pEventMsg)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Handles keyboard navigation events for a text list widget.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract widget pointer from event message\n2. Assert widget type is D2WIN_LIST (type 7)\n3. Skip processing if event is 0x102 (focus change)\n4. For Enter key (0x0d): Clear input, invoke active item callback if present\n5. For Up arrow (0x26): Navigate to previous item in linked list\n   a. If at first item, wrap to last item\n   b. Otherwise traverse backwards to find previous node\n   c. Recalculate selection index by counting from head\n   d. Adjust scroll position if needed\n6. For Down arrow (0x28): Navigate to next item in linked list\n   a. If at last item, wrap to first item\n   b. Set new active item and recalculate selection index\n   c. Adjust scroll position if needed\n7. For other key codes: Iterate item list checking for matching hotkey\n   - Compare event code against item's hotkey at offset 0x21c\n   - If match found and callback exists, invoke it\n\nParameters:\n- pEventMsg: Pointer to event message structure\n  - [0]: Pointer to ListWidget structure\n  - [1]: Event type (0x102 = focus change)\n  - [2]: Key code (0x0d=Enter, 0x26=Up, 0x28=Down, or hotkey)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Event was handled (navigation occurred)\n- 0: Event not handled (passed through)\n- callback result: If item callback was invoked\n\nWidget Structure (ListWidget) Offsets:\n- 0x00: Type (must be 7 for D2WIN_LIST)\n- 0x4c (0x13*4): Scroll top index\n- 0x54 (0x15*4): Selection index\n- 0x58 (0x16*4): Visible item count\n- 0x64 (0x19*4): List head pointer\n- 0x68 (0x1a*4): Active item pointer\n\nItem Structure Offsets:\n- 0x204: Item callback function pointer\n- 0x21c: Hotkey code (ushort)\n- 0x220: Next item pointer (linked list)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:cb2879b7d0e184d16335f5469d9475f2",
