      "name": "LinkObjectToList",
      "signature": "int LinkObjectToList(void * pObject)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Append object to linked list by traversing to tail node.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if list is empty (DAT_6f961528 == NULL)\n2. If empty, set as head and return 1\n3. If not empty, traverse to tail by following next pointers at offset 0x3c\n4. Append new object to tail's next pointer\n5. Return 1 (success)\n\nParameters:\n- pObject (void *): Pointer to object to append to list\n\nReturns:\n- 1 (success)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3c (60): Offset of next pointer in linked list node",
