      "name": "SetOrClearBitMask",
      "signature": "void SetOrClearBitMask(void * pData, int nBitSet)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Sets or clears a bit mask field within a data structure.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert pData is not NULL (triggers abort if NULL)\n2. If nBitSet is non-zero: OR the field at offset +8 with a bit mask\n3. If nBitSet is zero: AND the field at offset +8 with an inverted bit mask\n\nParameters:\n- pData (void*): Pointer to data structure (must not be NULL)\n- nBitSet (int): Flag indicating set (non-zero) or clear (zero) operation\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8 (8): Offset of bit mask field within structure\n- 0x2ed: Line number in source file for NULL assertion",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
