      "sizes": {
        "LoD/1.07": 120,
        "LoD/1.08": 120,
        "LoD/1.09": 120,
        "LoD/1.09b": 120,
        "LoD/1.09d": 120,
        "LoD/1.10": 120
      },
      "name": "ClampCursorToScreenBounds",
      "signature": "void ClampCursorToScreenBounds(dword * pScreenInfo)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Clamps cursor position to screen bounds and updates global screen dimensions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract max width from low 16 bits of pScreenInfo[3] (offset +0xC)\n2. Extract max height from high 16 bits of pScreenInfo[3]\n3. Call DispatchVirtualMethod to get current cursor position (X in pScreenInfo, Y in dwCursorY)\n4. Decrement both cursor coordinates by 1 (convert to 0-based)\n5. Call Ordinal_10047 (D2Gfx check) to verify graphics initialized\n6. If graphics not initialized, skip clamping logic\n7. Clamp X: if cursorX < maxWidth, use cursorX; else use maxWidth\n8. Clamp Y: if cursorY < maxHeight, use cursorY; else use maxHeight  \n9. If clamping occurred, call SetCursorPos to reposition cursor\n10. Store clamped Y in g_nScreenWidth global\n11. Store clamped X in g_nScreenHeight global\n\nParameters:\n  pScreenInfo - Pointer to screen info structure with packed dimensions at offset +0xC\n                Low 16 bits: max width, High 16 bits: max height\n\nReturns: void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - If Ordinal_10047 returns 0 (graphics not initialized), cursor is not clamped\n  - Cursor coordinates are decremented by 1 before bounds checking\n  - Note: g_nScreenWidth stores Y, g_nScreenHeight stores X (appears reversed)\n\nOrdinal Functions:\n  Ordinal_10047 - D2Gfx graphics initialization check",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:5b6889ef14ca451a6b917e368d655b60",
