      "name": "FindAndProcessCurrentInputItem",
      "signature": "void FindAndProcessCurrentInputItem(InventoryItem * pItem)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "FindAndProcessCurrentInputItem - Searches inventory linked list for current input item and processes it\n\nWARNING: Function body is truncated in Ghidra (only 1 instruction visible at 0x6f90f420).\nFull function spans 0x6f90f420-0x6f90f44a based on byte analysis. Manual repair required.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load g_dwCurrentInputItem into ECX\n2. If ECX is NULL, jump to step 7 (no current item)\n3. Load g_pLastInventoryItem (linked list head) into EAX\n4. If EAX is NULL, return without processing (empty list)\n5. Compare EAX with ECX - if match found, jump to step 7\n6. Walk linked list via pNext field (offset +0x3C) until match or NULL\n7. Push pItem parameter and call ProcessInventoryItems\n8. Return (RET 4 - stdcall cleanup)\n\nParameters:\n  pItem (InventoryItem *) - Item to process if current input item found in list\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nGlobals Referenced:\n  g_dwCurrentInputItem (0x6f96153c) - Current input item identifier\n  g_pLastInventoryItem (0x6f961540) - Head of inventory linked list\n\nStructure Access:\n  InventoryItem.pNext at offset +0x3C (60 bytes) - Next pointer in linked list\n\nCalled Functions:\n  ProcessInventoryItems (0x6f90f470) - Processes the inventory item\n\nClassification: Worker function - searches linked list and delegates to ProcessInventoryItems",
