      "name": "InitializeDialogControlByType",
      "signature": "void InitializeDialogControlByType(Control * pControl)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes specific dialog control types (0xF010, 0xF100, 0xF130) by setting enabled state.\n\nNOTE: Function boundaries incomplete in Ghidra. Actual function: 0x6f90f540-0x6f90f57C.\nFull implementation analyzed from raw bytes below.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load Control structure pointer from stack parameter\n2. Read type word from pControl+0x8\n3. Mask type with 0xFFF0 (ignores variant bits in lower nibble)\n4. Check if masked type matches: 0xF010, 0xF100, or 0xF130\n5. If no match, exit without modification\n6. Call Ordinal_10028 for validation/availability check\n7. If check fails (returns 0), exit without modification\n8. Set pControl+0x18 = 1 (enabled flag)\n9. Set pControl+0x1C = 0 (initial state)\n10. Return via RET 4 (stdcall cleanup)\n\nParameters:\npControl (Control *) - Pointer to dialog control structure with type at +0x8\n\nReturns:\nvoid - Modifies control structure in place if type matches criteria\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Only handles type codes 0xF010, 0xF100, 0xF130 (after 0xFFF0 mask)\n- Other control types pass through unchanged\n- Ordinal_10028 must return non-zero for initialization to occur\n\nStructure Layout (Control):\nOffset  Size  Field       Description\n0x08    2     wType       Control type code\n0x18    4     dwEnabled   Enable flag (set to 1)\n0x1C    4     dwState     State value (set to 0)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n0xFFF0 - Mask for type code (ignores lower 4 variant bits)\n0xF010 - Control type (scroll-like control)\n0xF100 - Control type (button-like control)\n0xF130 - Control type (edit-like control)",
