      "name": "UpdateMusicStateFromOptions",
      "signature": "void UpdateMusicStateFromOptions(AudioCookie * pAudioCookie)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Updates music playback state based on current audio options.\n\nClassification: Worker function - processes audio state changes\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if audio system is enabled (g_fAudioSystemEnabled)\n2. If disabled, return immediately without changes\n3. Call GetInitializedState to verify audio subsystem is ready\n4. If not initialized, return without changes\n5. Call GetMusicOptions to query current music configuration\n6. If options == 0: Call Ordinal_10034 (likely reset/default music)\n7. If options != 0: Call ProcessAudioQueue (apply music settings)\n8. Call SetMusicVolume to apply volume changes\n9. Set pAudioCookie->fUpdated = 1 (success flag)\n10. Set pAudioCookie->dwErrorCode = 0 (clear error)\n\nParameters:\n  pAudioCookie - AudioCookie* to audio state structure\n    +0x18 (fUpdated): uint - Success/updated flag (set to 1 on success)\n    +0x1c (dwErrorCode): uint - Error code (cleared to 0 on success)\n\nReturns:\n  void - no return value, state updated via pAudioCookie\n\nExternal Calls:\n  GetInitializedState (0x6f91c4de) - Check if audio system initialized\n  GetMusicOptions (0x6f91c4d8) - Get current music configuration\n  Ordinal_10034 (0x6f91c4cc) - Process default/reset music state\n  ProcessAudioQueue (0x6f91c4d2) - Apply queued music options\n  SetMusicVolume (0x6f91c4c6) - Apply volume settings\n\nGlobals:\n  g_fAudioSystemEnabled (0x6f961550) - Audio system enable flag\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Early exit if audio system disabled\n  - Early exit if audio not initialized\n  - Both flags updated atomically only on full success\n\nNotes:\n  - Orphan function (no callers detected)\n  - Function body malformed in Ghidra (single instruction)\n  - Actual extent: 0x6f90f940-0x6f90f98c (79 bytes)\n  - Uses __stdcall convention (RET 4)",
