      "name": "HandleMouseButtonMessage",
      "signature": "void HandleMouseButtonMessage(int * pMouseMsg)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Handles mouse button messages (WM_LBUTTONDOWN, WM_RBUTTONDOWN, WM_LBUTTONUP, WM_RBUTTONUP) by dispatching to UI controls.\n\nFUNCTION BOUNDARY WARNING: This function has incorrect boundaries in Ghidra (single instruction). The decompiler follows actual code flow but variables cannot be renamed via MCP.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract mouse X/Y coordinates from message LPARAM (low word = X, high word = Y)\n2. Call DispatchVirtualMethod to transform coordinates\n3. Adjust coordinates by -1 for screen mapping\n4. Call Ordinal_10047 (D2GFX check) to verify graphics active\n5. Clamp cursor position to screen bounds if needed via SetCursorPos\n6. Store cursor position to g_nScreenHeight/g_nScreenWidth globals\n7. Check if screen popup is active via IsScreenPopupActiveBitSet\n8. If popup active, invoke screen handler and process inventory, return if handled\n9. Get control list from g_dwLastInventoryItem or g_pInventoryList\n10. Switch on message type (pMouseMsg[1]):\n    - 0x201 (WM_LBUTTONDOWN) / 0x204 (WM_RBUTTONDOWN): Set g_dwGameState=1, iterate controls for hit-test and invoke button-down callback at offset +0x24\n    - 0x202 (WM_LBUTTONUP) / 0x205 (WM_RBUTTONUP): Set g_dwGameState=0, iterate controls and invoke button-up callback at offset +0x28\n11. Insert message cookie into cache via InsertCacheNodeWithCookie\n\nParameters:\n  pMouseMsg - Pointer to mouse message structure:\n    +0x00: Control pointer (set by handler)\n    +0x04: Message type (0x201-0x205)\n    +0x0C: LPARAM containing X/Y coordinates\n\nReturns: void\n\nControl Structure Offsets (UI Element):\n  +0x0C: nLeft (int) - Left boundary X coordinate\n  +0x10: nRight (int) - Right boundary X coordinate  \n  +0x14: nHeight (int) - Height of control\n  +0x18: nOffsetX (int) - Horizontal offset adjustment\n  +0x24: pfnOnMouseDown (code*) - Mouse down callback handler\n  +0x28: pfnOnMouseUp (code*) - Mouse up callback handler\n  +0x38: pfnHitTest (code*) - Custom hit-test callback (NULL for default bounds check)\n  +0x3C: pNextControl (ptr) - Next control in linked list\n\nMagic Numbers:\n  0x201 = WM_LBUTTONDOWN - Left mouse button pressed\n  0x202 = WM_LBUTTONUP - Left mouse button released\n  0x204 = WM_RBUTTONDOWN - Right mouse button pressed\n  0x205 = WM_RBUTTONUP - Right mouse button released\n\nGlobals Modified:\n  g_nScreenHeight - Current cursor Y position\n  g_nScreenWidth - Current cursor X position\n  g_dwGameState - Mouse button state (1=down, 0=up)\n  g_nCallbackDepth - Callback nesting depth counter\n\nDecompiler Variable Mapping (cannot rename due to boundary issue):\n  dwCookieValue -> pMouseMsg (saved parameter)\n  iVar1 -> nHandlerResult / pCurrentControl\n  iVar2 -> nCallbackResult\n  dVar3 -> nCursorX\n  uVar4 -> wMouseX (extracted X from LPARAM)\n  uVar5 -> wMouseY (extracted Y from LPARAM)\n  dVar6 -> nCursorY\n  dStack_4 -> nAdjustedY",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
