      "name": "SetUnitFlags",
      "signature": "void SetUnitFlags(uint * pUnit, int nMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Sets or clears a bit flag at offset +8 in a unit structure based on mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Test if nMode is non-zero\n2. If nMode != 0: OR the flag at pUnit+8 with mask from gdwBitMasks_exref[0xc]\n3. If nMode == 0: AND the flag at pUnit+8 with inverted mask from gdwInvBitMasks_exref[0xc]\n4. Return to caller\n\nParameters:\n- pUnit (uint*): Pointer to unit structure; flag value modified at offset +8\n- nMode (int): Mode selector: non-zero sets flag, zero clears flag\n\nReturns:\n- void; modifies unit structure in-place\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8: Offset of flag field within unit structure\n- 0xc: Offset within bit mask tables",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ea3c81bb2209264c7524cfa21507db6d",
