      "name": "InitializeScreenObject",
      "signature": "void InitializeScreenObject(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a screen object structure (1128 bytes). Sets default screen dimensions, flags, and event handlers. Returns pointer stored in global g_pCurrentScreenData.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if screen object already exists; if so, process and release it\n2. Allocate new structure (0x468 bytes) via FogMemAlloc\n3. Zero-fill entire structure using REP STOSD (282 dwords)\n4. Set object type field to 0xB\n5. Configure bit flags from gdwBitMasks_exref (3 flag sources)\n6. Store screen dimensions from globals g_nScreenHeight, g_nScreenWidth\n7. Install function pointers for event handlers at offsets [7] and [8]\n8. Initialize remaining fields to 0\n9. Link object to global list via LinkObjectToList\n10. Store reference in g_pCurrentScreenData\n\nParameters:\n- No explicit parameters\n- IMPLICIT: Uses global variables g_nScreenHeight, g_nScreenWidth, gdwBitMasks_exref\n\nReturns:\n- void (result stored in global g_pCurrentScreenData)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x468 (1128): Structure size in bytes\n- 0x11A (282): Number of dwords to zero-fill\n- 0xB: Screen object type constant\n- Offsets [2-0xD]: Structure field indices storing flags and dimensions",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:08afdcb93495a6ce28a8b7e68b713b6d",
