      "name": "IsScreenPopupActiveBitSet",
      "signature": "int IsScreenPopupActiveBitSet(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Checks if screen popup is active and specific bits are set.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if current screen data is initialized\n2. Assert screen type is popup (0xb)\n3. Test if both bit masks 0x0 and 0x8 are set in screen data[2]\n4. Return 1 if both bits set, 0 otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- None (uses global screen data)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if screen is popup and both active bits are set\n- 0 otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xb: Screen type for popup\n- 0x6f91d164: Pointer to bit masks array\n- 0x8: Offset to flags field in screen data",
