      "name": "TryInvokeScreenHandler",
      "signature": "int TryInvokeScreenHandler(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Attempts to invoke the current screen's event handler if conditions are met.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify current screen type is popup (0xb), assert otherwise\n2. Check if both bit flags in gdwBitMasks are set on g_pCurrentScreenData[2]\n3. Verify screen has a valid handler index (g_pCurrentScreenData[0x119] != -1)\n4. Calculate handler function pointer from screen data using stride 0x21 (33) bytes\n5. If pointer is non-null, invoke it and return 1, otherwise return 0\n\nParameters:\n- None\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if handler was invoked\n- 0 if conditions not met or handler pointer is null",
