      "name": "AllocateAndInitializeObject",
      "signature": "void AllocateAndInitializeObject(uint dwParam1, uint dwParam2, uint dwParam3, uint dwParam4)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a 0x44-byte object structure with parameters and flags.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate 0x44 bytes via FogMemAlloc\n2. Zero-initialize entire structure (0x11 dwords)\n3. Set offset 0x0 to 10\n4. OR bit flags from gdwBitMasks_exref into offsets 0x8 and 0x8 again with additional mask\n5. Store parameters at offsets 0xc, 0x10, 0x14, 0x18\n6. Store callback function pointer at offset 0x1c\n7. Zero remaining fields\n8. Link object to global list via LinkObjectToList\n9. Return allocated and initialized object\n\nParameters:\n- nParam1 (uint): Parameter stored at offset 0xc\n- nParam2 (uint): Parameter stored at offset 0x10\n- nParam3 (uint): Parameter stored at offset 0x14\n- nParam4 (uint): Parameter stored at offset 0x18\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated and initialized 0x44-byte object structure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
