      "name": "ScrollbarAdjustPosition",
      "signature": "int ScrollbarAdjustPosition(int nScrollbar, int * pScrollbarData, int nDelta)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Adjusts scrollbar position by a delta value and enforces bounds.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Verify scrollbar structure type is valid, abort if not\n2. Return early if scrollbar is disabled (eType == 0x16)\n3. Adjust position based on nDelta: set flag if negative (up/back) or positive (down/forward)\n4. Add/subtract delta from current position field (offset 0x13)\n5. Clamp position to valid range: [0, max_position at offset 0x12]\n6. Execute optional position change callback if pointer at offset 0x15 exists\n7. Execute optional custom callback if function pointer at offset 0x17 exists\n\nParameters:\n- pScrollbar (int): Scrollbar handle/context (passed via ECX)\n- pScrollbarData (int *): Pointer to scrollbar structure (D2WIN_SCROLLBAR)\n- nDelta (int): Position delta (positive = forward/down, negative = back/up)\n\nReturns:\n- 0 (success)\n\nStructure Layout (pScrollbarData offsets):\n- 0x13 (19): Current position (clamped)\n- 0x12 (18): Maximum position\n- 0x10 (16): Forward flag\n- 0x11 (17): Backward flag\n- 0x15 (21): Position change callback\n- 0x16 (22): Disabled flag\n- 0x17 (23): Custom change callback",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:088648e0c373989a3d736e6382517fa8",
