      "name": "CreateUIObject",
      "signature": "int * CreateUIObject(int nType, int nFlags, int nX, int nY, int nWidth, int nHeight, int nParent, int nControlCode, dword dwOptions, int * pInitialValues, int * pCustomData)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Creates and initializes a UI object with specified properties.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocates 0xA8 bytes (42 dwords) for the object structure\n2. Zero-initializes all fields via REP STOSD loop\n3. Applies locale-specific font sizing (CJK languages 7,9)\n4. For scrollbar objects, creates scrollbar child and computes row height\n5. Links object into global list and returns pointer\n\nParameters:\n- nType (ECX): Object type identifier\n- nFlags (EDX): Flag bits controlling behavior\n- nX, nY: Position coordinates\n- nWidth, nHeight: Dimensions\n- nParent: Parent object handle\n- nControlCode: Control/message identifier\n- dwOptions: Option flags (0x1=flag, 0x4=scrollbar)\n- pInitialValues: Optional initial state array\n- pCustomData: Optional custom parameters\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocated UI object on success\n- Asserts on critical allocation failures",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:de729157f63f61883be71095c9dfa74c",
