      "name": "AddTextLines",
      "signature": "uint AddTextLines(void * pptxTextObject, wchar_t * wszDisplayText, int nLineCount, uint dwFlags, byte bUnknown)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Adds text lines to a UI text object with proper layout and CJK font height handling.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input: Ensure text object pointer is non-null and type field equals 4\n2. Calculate Unicode string length for buffer allocation\n3. Loop for each requested line count\n4. Allocate 0x20-byte text entry structure and string buffer (length * 2 + 2 bytes)\n5. Copy Unicode string into allocated buffer\n6. Initialize entry fields: string pointer, 4x uint fields (cleared), flags, control byte, padding\n7. Link entry into text object's linked list structure\n8. Increment text object's line counter\n9. If rendering enabled, calculate layout offset based on locale-specific font height\n10. Invoke text layout update with calculated line offset\n\nParameters:\n- pptxTextObject (void*): Text UI object structure\n- wszDisplayText (wchar_t*): Unicode display string\n- nLineCount (int): Number of lines to add\n- dwFlags (uint): Text entry configuration flags\n- bUnknown (byte): Control byte stored in entry[6]\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on success\n- Never returns on validation failure (assertion failure)",
