      "name": "TextBox_SetNumColumns",
      "signature": "void TextBox_SetNumColumns(int * ptTextData, int nNumColumns)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Sets the number of columns for a TextBox control.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate ptTextData is not NULL (assert failure if NULL)\n2. Validate ptTextData->eType == 4 (D2WIN_TEXTBOX type check)\n3. Validate nNumColumns is in range (0 < nNumColumns < 6)\n4. Validate nNumColumns >= current column count (cannot reduce columns)\n5. Set ptTextData->nNumColumns = nNumColumns (offset 0x64)\n6. If nNumColumns > 1, set multi-column flag (bit 0x20 at offset 0x5C)\n\nParameters:\n  ptTextData (ECX) - Pointer to TextData structure, must be type D2WIN_TEXTBOX (4)\n  nNumColumns (EDX) - Number of columns to set (valid range: 1-5 inclusive)\n\nReturns:\n  void - No return value; function asserts on invalid input\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - NULL ptTextData triggers assert at line 0x2A6\n  - Wrong type (eType != 4) triggers assert at line 0x2A7\n  - nNumColumns out of range triggers assert at line 0x2A9\n  - Reducing column count triggers assert at line 0x2AB\n\nStructure Layout (TextData):\n  Offset  Size  Field           Type    Description\n  0x00    4     eType           int     Control type (4 = D2WIN_TEXTBOX)\n  0x5C    4     dwFlags         uint    Control flags (bit 0x20 = multi-column)\n  0x64    4     nNumColumns     int     Number of columns (1-5)\n\nFlag Bits (dwFlags at offset 0x5C):\n  0x20 - Multi-column mode enabled (set when nNumColumns > 1)\n\nOrdinal: 10056",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:3bc41fff3298c1e9978da2532ef2748a",
