      "name": "TEXTBOX_SetColumnValue",
      "signature": "void TEXTBOX_SetColumnValue(int * ptTextData, int nColumn, int nValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "TEXTBOX_SetColumnValue - Sets a column value in a D2WIN textbox control.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate ptTextData is non-NULL (assert \"hChild\" on failure)\n2. Validate ptTextData->eType == D2WIN_TEXTBOX (type 4) (assert \"ptTextData->eType == D2WIN_TEXTBOX\" on failure)\n3. Validate column index bounds: (nColumn >= 0) && (nColumn < ptTextData->nNumColumns)\n4. Store nValue at ptTextData->aColumnValues[nColumn] (offset 0x68 + nColumn*4)\n\nParameters:\n  ptTextData (ECX) - Pointer to TextData/UI control structure, must be type D2WIN_TEXTBOX (4)\n  nColumn (EDX) - Zero-based column index, must be in range [0, nNumColumns)\n  nValue (stack +4) - Value to store in the specified column\n\nReturns:\n  void - Function does not return on assertion failure\n\nStructure Layout (TextData):\n  Offset  Size  Field          Description\n  0x00    4     eType          Control type (must be 4 for TEXTBOX)\n  0x64    4     nNumColumns    Number of columns in this textbox\n  0x68    N*4   aColumnValues  Array of column values (indexed by nColumn)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- NULL ptTextData triggers assertion with message \"hChild\"\n- Wrong control type triggers assertion with message \"ptTextData->eType == D2WIN_TEXTBOX\"\n- Out-of-bounds column triggers assertion with message \"( nColumn >= 0 ) && ( nColumn < ptTextData->nNumColumns )\"\n- All assertion failures call AssertFailure(-1) which does not return\n\nError Handling:\n  Uses FogAssert + AssertFailure pattern for debug validation\n  Line numbers from D2Win source: 0x2B8 (696), 0x2B9 (697), 0x2BB (699)",
