      "name": "ProcessTimerKeyCallback",
      "signature": "int ProcessTimerKeyCallback(int * pTimerData)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Processes timer key callback events for timer data objects.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate timer data type equals D2WIN_TIMER (8) via assertion\n2. Check if message is not WM_KEYDOWN (0x102) AND event type is 0x20 (KEY_DOWN)\n3. If conditions pass, retrieve callback pointer from timer vtable offset 0xd\n4. If callback exists (non-null), invoke callback with timer data\n5. Return 1 if callback was invoked, 0 otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- pTimerData: Pointer to timer data structure (72-byte object from CreateObjectInstance)\n  - [0]: Pointer to vtable/type structure (must point to value 8)\n  - [1]: Message type (0x102 = WM_KEYDOWN excluded)\n  - [2]: Event flags (0x20 = KEY_DOWN event)\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Callback was invoked successfully\n- 0: Conditions not met (wrong message type or no callback)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Asserts if timer type != 8 (D2WIN_TIMER), indicating corrupted timer data\n- Callback at vtable offset 0xd was stored from nCallback in CreateObjectInstance\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x8: D2WIN_TIMER type identifier\n- 0x102: WM_KEYDOWN message (excluded from processing)\n- 0x20: KEY_DOWN event flag\n- 0xd: Vtable offset for user callback function pointer",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:dca9876e01c8729a6a4839ef10e6ca3d",
