      "name": "DispatchCacheOperation",
      "signature": "void DispatchCacheOperation(void * pCache, uint dwOperation, int nMessageId, uint dwParam)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "Dispatches cache operations based on operation type.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Assert pCache is not null\n2. Switch on dwOperation: 0=validate message, 1=SMemCache, 2=SmxEntry, 3=ImisCache\n3. For dwOperation 1-3: invoke corresponding handler with nMessageId and dwParam\n4. For dwOperation 0: validate nMessageId against forbidden Windows messages\n5. Assert failure if nMessageId is WM_COMMAND(0x111), WM_KEYUP(0x101), or WM_KEYDOWN(0x100)\n6. Otherwise route to ValidateAndRemoveCacheEntry_GSMS\n\nParameters:\n- pCache (void*): Opaque cache handle passed to handlers\n- dwOperation (uint): Operation type (0=validate, 1=SMemCache, 2=Smx, 3=Imis)\n- nMessageId (int): Windows message ID to process\n- dwParam (uint): Additional parameter for cache handler\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x100: WM_KEYDOWN message ID (forbidden in operation 0)\n- 0x101: WM_KEYUP message ID (forbidden in operation 0)\n- 0x111: WM_COMMAND message ID (forbidden in operation 0)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "API",
      "index": "API:b79292d94e16ef34794fd938eed8c42e",
