      "name": "GetFirstSetBitPosition",
      "signature": "int GetFirstSetBitPosition(dword dwValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Returns one-based bit position of the first set bit in a value.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if input value is zero, return 0 if true\n2. Use BSF (Bit Scan Forward) instruction to find lowest set bit position (0-based)\n3. Increment result by 1 to convert to one-based indexing\n4. Return the bit position\n\nParameters:\n- dwValue (dword): The value to scan for set bits\n\nReturns:\n- 1-32: One-based bit position of first set bit\n- 0: If input value is zero\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- Bit positions are 1-based (bit 0 = position 1)\n- BSF result is 0-based (bit 0 = position 0)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:eec0749ef2bff57a0570b6bf799026d4",
