      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Process exit handlers and terminate process.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Call FUN_6f914443 initialization\n2. If global exit flag set, terminate process immediately with dwExitCode\n3. Set exit state globals (nExitCode, nExitMode)\n4. If nMode == 0, invoke registered exit handler chain (backward iteration)\n5. Call cleanup functions for standard/custom resources\n6. If nCode == 0, set flag and exit process; otherwise cleanup and return\n\nParameters:\n- dwExitCode (uint): Exit code for process termination\n- nMode (int): Exit mode (0=normal, non-zero=abnormal)\n- nCode (int): Control code (0=exit, non-zero=continue)\n\nReturns:\n- void (terminates process if nCode==0, otherwise returns normally)",
