      "name": "ProbeStackPages",
      "signature": "void ProbeStackPages(dword nStackSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Probes stack pages to prevent stack overflow exception on large allocations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get return address from stack\n2. Calculate probe pointer at [ESP + 8] (after PUSH ECX)\n3. While allocation size > 4KB (0x1000):\n   - Probe (TEST) current page\n   - Move probe pointer back 4KB\n   - Decrement allocation size by 4KB\n4. Probe final partial page\n5. Adjust ESP to new top of stack\n6. Restore registers and return\n\nParameters:\n- nStackSize (EAX): Size of stack space to probe in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- void (stack pointer adjusted to new location)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1000 (4096): Page size",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:2a518bd4b0b93e6cf2e2d91eb6ff7bf6",
