      "name": "MemMove",
      "signature": "void * MemMove(void * pDest, void * pSrc, uint dwBytes)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Overlapping-aware memory copy (memmove equivalent).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if source overlaps destination (src < dest < src+size)\n2. If overlapping: copy backward from end to start\n3. If non-overlapping: copy forward from start to end\n4. Optimize alignment: copy dwords when possible, handle unaligned tails\n5. Unroll loops: process in 8-dword chunks for performance\n\nParameters:\n- pDest (void*): Destination buffer\n- pSrc (void*): Source buffer\n- nBytes (uint): Number of bytes to copy\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to destination buffer\n\nNotes:\n- Handles overlapping source/destination correctly\n- Uses dword copies when alignment permits (unroll 8)\n- Falls back to byte copies for unaligned regions",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:bff09423b51fd121ea30afec957819f4",
