      "name": "InitializeModule",
      "signature": "uint InitializeModule(uint dwUnused, int nMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Manages module initialization and cleanup lifecycle based on operation mode.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Mode 1 (Initialize): Retrieve system version, verify platform prerequisites, extract version components (major/minor), initialize subsystems via helper functions, increment init counter, retrieve command line\n2. Mode 0 (Cleanup): Decrement init counter; if counter reaches 0, perform full cleanup (close resources, cleanup handlers, shutdown subsystems)\n3. Mode 3 (Special): Call specialized handler with NULL parameter\n4. All modes: Return success/failure status to caller\n\nParameters:\n- dwUnused (uint): Reserved parameter for future use (not utilized in current implementation)\n- nMode (int): Operation mode - 1 (initialize), 0 (cleanup), 3 (special handler)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on successful operation or if module already initialized\n- 0 on initialization failure or if cleanup attempted on uninitialized module",
