      "name": "CleanupCriticalSections",
      "signature": "void CleanupCriticalSections(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Destroys all critical sections used for thread synchronization.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Iterate through critical section array starting at g_ppCriticalSections\n2. For each critical section pointer encountered before g_pCriticalSection1:\n   - Skip if NULL pointer\n   - Skip if pointer matches one of the special critical sections (g_pCriticalSection1-3 or g_pCriticalSectionArray)\n   - Delete the critical section with DeleteCriticalSection()\n   - Call cleanup handler FUN_6f916a9e() on the section\n3. Increment pointer by 4 bytes and continue until reaching g_pCriticalSectionArray end\n4. Explicitly delete the four special critical sections\n\nParameters:\n- None\n\nReturns:\n- void (implicit EDI = DeleteCriticalSection function pointer loaded from [0x6f91d264])",
