      "name": "TransformCharacterWithFlags",
      "signature": "dword TransformCharacterWithFlags(void * this, void * pThis, int nCharCode, dword dwMask)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Transforms a character code using the character transformation table with a bitmask.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if character code is in valid range (0-256)\n2. If in range, look up transformed value from table directly\n3. If out of range, check high byte flag in table for multi-byte transformation\n4. If flag set, construct 2-byte transform data and call handler; otherwise 1-byte\n5. AND result with provided bitmask and return\n\nParameters:\n- pThis (void*): Context pointer\n- nCharCode (int): Character code to transform\n- dwMask (dword): Bitmask to apply to result\n\nReturns:\n- Transformed character value masked with dwMask, or 0 on transform failure",
