      "name": "BufferWriteByte",
      "signature": "dword BufferWriteByte(dword byteValue, int * pBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Write a byte value to a buffer, handling buffer state transitions and overflow conditions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract buffer state flags from pBuffer[3]\n2. If buffer is uninitialized (flags & 0x82 == 0) or already has data flag (flags & 0x40), set DATA_PRESENT flag\n3. Otherwise, handle existing data:\n   - If current pointer at start (flags & 1), reset buffer to beginning\n   - Mark buffer modified (flags &= ~0x1)\n   - Clear flags indicating data state, set modified flag (flags |= 0x2)\n4. If buffer is not protected (!(flags & 0x10c)), validate buffer node:\n   - Skip special nodes (g_pDefaultBufferNode1, g_pDefaultBufferNode2)\n   - Call validation function if conditions met\n5. Write byte:\n   - If write area is empty, allocate from buffer pool\n   - Otherwise append to existing data\n6. Return byte value if write succeeds, 0xFFFFFFFF if fails\n\nParameters:\n- byteValue (dword): Byte to write (masked to 0xFF)\n- pBuffer (int*): Pointer to buffer node structure\n\nReturns:\n- 0xFF if write succeeds\n- 0xFFFFFFFF on failure",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:28393cf54a38bf1465f92d01d5d4df21",
