      "signature": "int SprintfxVa(int * pBuffer, byte * pFormat, int * pVaList)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Format string processing engine for sprintfx family.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse format string byte by byte, using state machine (g_abStateTable)\n2. For each format specifier, extract modifiers (flags, width, precision)\n3. Process conversion specifiers (d,i,u,x,X,o,c,s,S,p,n,e,E,f,F,g,G)\n4. Handle width/precision padding with spaces and zeros\n5. Output formatted data via buffer callback (param_1)\n6. Return total characters output in pBuffer[0]\n\nParameters:\n- pBuffer (int*): Output buffer control block (pBuffer[0]=callback routine)\n- pFormat (byte*): Format string in ASCII (null-terminated)\n- pVaList (int*): Variable argument list pointer array\n\nReturns:\n- Count of characters written to output buffer\n\nFlag Bits (dwFlags/local_8):\n- 0x001: Force sign (+)\n- 0x002: Space padding for positives\n- 0x004: Left-align (negate 0x008)\n- 0x008: Zero-pad\n- 0x010: Short integer (h modifier)\n- 0x020: Char conversion or unsigned short\n- 0x040: Float/double conversion (e,E,f,F,g,G)\n- 0x080: # modifier (alternate form)\n- 0x100: Negative value flag (internal)\n- 0x200: Octal alternate (0 prefix)\n- 0x800: Wide character (w modifier)\n- 0x1000: Uppercase hex\n- 0x8000: 64-bit integer (I64 modifier)\n\nState Machine (g_abStateTable):\n- State 0: Initial, output literal characters\n- State 1: Start format specifier (%)\n- State 2: Parse flags (-, +, space, #, 0)\n- State 3: Parse width or * wildcard\n- State 4: Period before precision\n- State 5: Parse precision digits or * wildcard\n- State 6: Length modifiers (h, l, L, w, I64)\n- State 7: Conversion specifier (d, s, f, etc)\n\nRelated: ProcessBufferCleanup, FUN_6f9159fa (va_arg), _strlen",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:b7a52aed3655c7d65807498f610c8ff8",
