      "name": "WriteCharacterRepeated",
      "signature": "void WriteCharacterRepeated(uint dwByteChar, int nCount, int * pBuffer, int * pStatus)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Outputs a single character repeated multiple times to a formatted output buffer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Loop while nCount > 0, decrementing nCount each iteration\n2. Call sub-function to write byChar to buffer\n3. Check for write error (*pStatus == -1) and exit early if detected\n\nParameters:\n- byChar (uint): Character to output (0x00-0xFF)\n- nCount (int): Number of times to repeat the character\n- pBuffer (int*): Output buffer state/context pointer\n- pStatus (int*): Output status; incremented on each write, set to -1 on error\n\nReturns:\n- void; status reported via *pStatus output parameter",
