      "signature": "char * FormatDoubleToString(double * pdblValue, char * pszBuffer, int nWidth, int nFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts a double-precision floating-point number to a formatted string representation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract lower and upper 32-bits of the double value\n2. Format the mantissa and exponent into local buffers\n3. Adjust output buffer pointer based on sign and field width\n4. Write the formatted digits to the output buffer\n\nParameters:\n- pdblValue (double*): Pointer to the double value to convert\n- pszBuffer (char*): Output buffer for the formatted string\n- nWidth (int): Minimum field width for output (0 or positive)\n- nFlags (int): Format flags controlling precision and notation\n\nReturns:\n- char*: Pointer to the output buffer (same as pszBuffer)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:9d2a5d769a01e278db09b78de631f581",
