      "name": "FormatExponentString",
      "signature": "BYTE * FormatExponentString(BYTE * pbBuffer, int nDigitCount, int nExponent, int * pnExponentState, char cNegative)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Formats floating-point number in exponential notation (e.g., \"1.23e+045\").\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If cNegative flag set, prepend '-' sign to buffer\n2. If nDigitCount > 0, move first digit to output position and place swap character (g_byCharacterSwapValue)\n3. Call FUN_6f916ea0 to append exponent string \"e+000\" to buffer\n4. If nExponent != 0, write 'E' marker and format exponent digits (hundreds, tens, ones)\n5. Return pointer to start of buffer\n\nParameters:\n- pbBuffer (BYTE*): Output string buffer for exponential format\n- nDigitCount (int): Number of significant digits to format\n- nExponent (int): Exponent value to append\n- pnExponentState (int*): Exponent state flags [0]=sign mode, [1]=exponent value, [3]=digits ready\n- cNegative (char): Non-zero if number is negative (adds leading '-')\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to pbBuffer (input buffer)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
