      "name": "FormatNumberString",
      "signature": "char * FormatNumberString(char * szBuffer, size_t nDecimalPlaces, int * pnValues, char cCondition)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Formats a numeric value into a string with sign, decimal point, and zero-padding.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If condition flag set and decimal places equals remaining string length, append '0' and null terminator\n2. If value is negative (0x2d = '-'), prepend '-' to output string\n3. If decimal places < 1, write '0' at current position and advance pointer\n4. Otherwise advance pointer by decimal places count\n5. If decimal places > 0, write decimal separator character at current position\n6. If decimal places < 0 (fractional part), fill remaining positions with padding zeros\n\nParameters:\n- szBuffer (char*): Output string buffer\n- nDecimalPlaces (size_t): Decimal point position or count\n- pnValues (int*): Array containing [sign_value, decimal_position]\n- fCondition (char): Flag controlling null-termination behavior\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to szBuffer (start of formatted string)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:1d26a9e5ce55b73c17db6b9f60fe2994",
