      "name": "CleanupThreadLocalStorage",
      "signature": "void CleanupThreadLocalStorage(void * pTlsData)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Cleans up thread-local storage by destructing pointers.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if TLS index is valid (not 0xFFFFFFFF)\n2. Get TLS data pointer from parameter or from TlsGetValue()\n3. For each cleanup pointer offset (0x24, 0x28, 0x30, 0x38, 0x40, 0x44, 0x50):\n   - Read pointer from structure\n   - If non-NULL and not the function table, call cleanup function\n4. Call cleanup on the structure itself\n5. Clear TLS value via TlsSetValue(0)\n\nParameters:\n- pTlsData (void*): TLS data structure pointer; if NULL, retrieves from TlsGetValue()\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwThreadLocalStorageIndex contains TLS slot index\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24, 0x28, 0x30, 0x38, 0x40, 0x44, 0x50: Offsets to cleanup pointers in structure\n- 0xFFFFFFFF: Invalid TLS index sentinel",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
