      "name": "InitializeStdioHandles",
      "signature": "void InitializeStdioHandles(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes standard I/O handle tables from startup info.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Allocate primary buffer table (0x480 bytes) storing 288 handle entry slots\n2. Initialize each slot: set handle to 0xffffffff, flags to 0, reserve byte to 10\n3. Call GetStartupInfoA to retrieve inherited startup parameters\n4. If startup info provides inherited handles, process each via GetFileType\n5. Allocate extended buffers if inherited handle count exceeds 288\n6. Initialize extended buffer entries with same default values\n7. Map each inherited handle to appropriate table entry based on handle index\n8. For stdin/stdout/stderr (indices 0-2), retrieve via GetStdHandle\n9. Validate file types and set appropriate flags (regular/pipe/device)\n10. Call SetHandleCount to register total handle count with runtime\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwHandleLimit (initial handle limit, incremented as buffers allocated)\n- IMPLICIT: g_pBufferTable (main handle table allocated by _malloc)\n- IMPLICIT: g_pBufferTableExtended (extended buffer pointers for overflow)\n\nReturns:\n- void (initializes global handle management structures)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x480: Bytes per handle buffer (288 entries * 4 bytes + 96 overhead)\n- 0x120: Maximum entries per primary buffer table\n- 0x7ff: Maximum inherited handle count (2047)\n- 0x800: Clamped handle limit (2048)\n- 0x20: Initial handle increment (32 entries)\n- 0xffffffff: Sentinel for uninitialized handle slot",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:1352fc0555ea3629db2c9325fd0e6c42",
