      "name": "InitializeModuleData",
      "signature": "void InitializeModuleData(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes module item data structures.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if module is already initialized (g_fInitialized)\n2. Get module file path via GetModuleFileNameA\n3. Use command line path if available, otherwise use module path\n4. First scan to count items and determine buffer size\n5. Allocate buffer for item data (size = nItemCount * 4 + nBufferSize)\n6. Second scan to populate item pointers and data\n7. Store global references to item array and count\n\nParameters:\n- void: No parameters (uses global state)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x104: Path buffer size (260 bytes)\n- 4: Bytes per item reference\n- -1: Item count adjustment for array indexing",
