      "name": "ParseCommandLine",
      "signature": "void ParseCommandLine(byte * pbInputString, uint * * ppdwArgumentPtrs, byte * pbOutputBuffer, int * pnInputLength, int * pnArgumentCount)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Parses a command-line string into individual arguments, handling quoted strings and escape sequences.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize output length counter to 0, argument count to 1\n2. If argument pointers array exists, store initial output buffer pointer\n3. Parse input string character by character:\n   - If string starts with quote (0x22), extract quoted substring handling escapes\n   - Otherwise parse unquoted substring until space/tab/null terminator\n   - Backslash (0x5c) escapes the next character when not in quotes\n   - Special handling for escaped quotes: pair of quotes when escaping active\n4. Build individual argument strings in output buffer with null terminators\n5. Store pointers to each argument in argument pointer array\n6. Return via output parameters\n\nParameters:\n- pbInputString (byte*): Command-line string to parse\n- ppdwArgumentPtrs (uint**): Array of pointers to parsed arguments (optional, NULL to skip)\n- pbOutputBuffer (byte*): Buffer for parsed argument strings (optional, NULL to skip writing)\n- pnInputLength (int*): Returns count of characters consumed from input\n- pnArgumentCount (int*): Returns count of arguments parsed\n\nReturns:\n- void (results via output parameters)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x22 (34): Double-quote character\n- 0x20 (32): Space character\n- 0x9 (9): Tab character\n- 0x5c (92): Backslash escape character\n- 0x4: Character class flag (special/escape-able character)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:50cd6b6fd69b78c0380659763fce7ea0",
