      "name": "GetCachedEnvironmentStrings",
      "signature": "LPSTR GetCachedEnvironmentStrings(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Retrieves cached environment strings, converting Unicode to ANSI on first call.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check static flag g_dwEnvStringState to determine which encoding is active\n2. If flag=0, try GetEnvironmentStringsW() and cache wide strings\n3. Convert wide strings to ANSI using WideCharToMultiByte()\n4. If flag=2, use GetEnvironmentStrings() for ANSI directly\n5. Return pointer to allocated buffer containing environment strings\n\nParameters:\n- NONE: No parameters\n\nReturns:\n- LPSTR: Pointer to environment string buffer (heap-allocated), NULL if failure",
