      "name": "ExtractPEHeaderMagic",
      "signature": "void ExtractPEHeaderMagic(byte * pbOutputBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Extracts PE header magic bytes from the loaded module base address.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Clear the output buffer to 0\n2. Get the current module handle (base address)\n3. Verify the module starts with MZ header (0x5a4d)\n4. Read the PE offset from DOS header offset 0x3c (at module+0xf*4)\n5. If valid, extract bytes at PE offset +2 and +3 into output buffer\n\nParameters:\n- pbOutputBuffer (undefined1 *): Output buffer for 2 PE header magic bytes\n\nReturns:\n- void (output written to pbOutputBuffer)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x5a4d: DOS MZ header signature\n- 0x3c / 0xf*4: Offset to PE header pointer in DOS header\n- +2, +3: PE signature bytes in PE header",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d8be7433da8984a6d08ceacc3367b90b",
