      "name": "InitializeHeapConfiguration",
      "signature": "int InitializeHeapConfiguration(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Initializes heap configuration based on OS version and environment variables.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Query OS version with GetVersionExA\n2. Return 2 if OS version < 5 (Windows 2000 or older)\n3. Check __MSVCRT_HEAP_SELECT environment variable\n4. If not set, extract heap mode from PE header\n5. Return 1 (standard), 2 (debug), or 3 (PE-based)\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: EBX contains heap configuration context\n\nReturns:\n- 1 (standard heap)\n- 2 (debug/special heap)\n- 3 (PE header-extracted configuration)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- ExtractPEHeaderMagic: Extracts heap mode from PE header\n- FUN_6f918eda: Processes heap configuration string",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:854e75bd7977160757e99400a787fb69",
