      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Executes exit cleanup handlers when process termination is initiated.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if initialization state is 1 or (state is 0 and termination flag is 1)\n2. If condition met, call cleanup routine with 0xfc (finalize)\n3. Execute registered exit callback if non-null\n4. Call cleanup routine again with 0xff (terminate)\n\nParameters:\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwInitializeState - Process initialization state (1=initialized)\n- IMPLICIT: g_dwTerminationFlag - Termination flag (1=terminate)\n- IMPLICIT: g_pfnExitCallback - Optional callback function pointer\n\nReturns:\n- void; executes cleanup routines but no return value used",
