      "name": "CleanupHeapBlock",
      "signature": "void CleanupHeapBlock(void * pBlock)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Cleans up a heap-allocated memory block during process cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return immediately if pBlock is NULL\n2. Check g_dwCleanupMode value:\n   - Mode 3: Acquire critical section 9, call FUN_6f919298 to get table, process with FUN_6f9192c3 if found, release section with FUN_6f916b08\n   - Mode 2: Acquire critical section 9, call FUN_6f919ff3 to get table and size, process with FUN_6f91a04a if found, release section with FUN_6f916b60\n   - Other: Skip to heap free\n3. Free the block with HeapFree if no cleanup was performed or completed\n\nParameters:\n- pBlock (void*): Pointer to heap block to clean up\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CleanupBufferTables, CleanupThreadLocalStorage (callers)\n- CleanupCriticalSections (related cleanup function)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:38a52ad8d9123a0ed65e4de10b1cf943",
