      "name": "AllocMemoryWithCleanup",
      "signature": "void * AllocMemoryWithCleanup(uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates memory from heap with cleanup mode support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Setup SEH exception handler frame to protect allocation\n2. Check g_dwCleanupMode value for cleanup strategy\n3. If mode 3: acquire critical section 9, use FUN_6f9195ec for allocation\n4. If mode 2: align size to 16-byte boundary, use FUN_6f91a08f, shift by 4\n5. Otherwise: fallthrough to standard HeapAlloc\n6. Cleanup critical section and restore exception list on success\n\nParameters:\n- dwSize (uint): Requested allocation size in bytes\n- IMPLICIT: EBX contains heap context pointer\n\nReturns:\n- void *: Pointer to allocated memory block from g_hHeap\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xf: 15-byte mask used with addition for rounding\n- 0xfffffff0: 16-byte alignment mask\n- 0x10: Minimum 16-byte allocation unit\n- 0xffffffff: Exception state sentinel value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
