      "name": "FindFirstCharNotInSet",
      "signature": "int FindFirstCharNotInSet(byte * pbSource, byte * pbCharset)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Finds the position of first character in pbSource that is NOT in pbCharset.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Build a bitset (abyCharMap) from all characters in pbCharset\n2. Scan pbSource sequentially, checking if each character is in the bitset\n3. Return index when first character NOT in set is found, or total length if all found\n\nParameters:\n- pbSource: Input string to search\n- pbCharset: String of characters to match against\n\nReturns:\n- Index of first char not in charset\n- Length of pbSource if all characters found in pbCharset\n\nNotes:\n- Uses byte-indexed bitset for O(1) lookup per character\n- Bitwise operations: (byte >> 3) = byte offset, (byte & 7) = bit position within byte",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:30f0fd08cad97c1e8bd24ed371c4d8a2",
