      "name": "CopyStringAligned",
      "signature": "char * CopyStringAligned(char * szDest, char * szSrc)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Copies a null-terminated string from source to destination using optimized word-aligned copying.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Align source pointer to 4-byte boundary by copying bytes\n2. Copy 4-byte chunks while looking for null terminator\n3. Detect null in chunk using formula: ~(chunk ^ 0xFFFFFFFF ^ chunk + 0x7EFEFEFF) & 0x81010100\n4. When null detected, copy remaining bytes and return\n\nParameters:\n- pszDest (char*): Destination buffer for string copy\n- pszSrc (char*): Source string to copy (null-terminated)\n\nReturns:\n- char*: Pointer to pszDest",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
