      "name": "CopyStringUnaligned",
      "signature": "dword * CopyStringUnaligned(dword * pszDest, dword * pszSrc)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Copies null-terminated string from source to destination, handling unaligned pointers efficiently.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Align destination pointer by copying bytes until 4-byte aligned\n2. Scan source with word-wide NULL checks using the formula (x ^ -1 ^ (x + 0x7efefeff)) & 0x81010100\n3. Copy aligned words from source, detecting partial NULLs byte-by-byte\n4. Null-terminate destination and return original destination pointer\n\nParameters:\n- pszDest (uint*): Destination buffer pointer (treated as byte array)\n- pszSrc (uint*): Source string pointer (treated as byte array)\n\nReturns:\n- Original destination pointer (pszDest)\n\nNotes:\n- Uses Knuth-Morris-Pratt-style NULL detection to scan 4 bytes at once\n- Handles misaligned source/destination pointers correctly\n- Returns destination for potential chaining",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:845fc5044ff181fe96e2ae868d3aa1f6",
