      "name": "MemCopyEx",
      "signature": "void * MemCopyEx(void * pdwDest, void * pdwSrc, dword nBytes)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Copies memory from source to destination, handling overlapping regions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if regions overlap (param_2 < param_1 AND param_1 < param_2+size)\n2. If overlapping: copy backward from end to start to avoid corruption\n3. If non-overlapping: copy forward from start to end\n4. Align copies to 4-byte boundaries for efficiency\n5. Use DWORD copies when possible, handle remaining bytes individually\n6. For unaligned destinations: handle misalignment in 1-3 byte increments first\n\nParameters:\n- pdwDest (void*): Destination buffer pointer\n- pdwSrc (void*): Source buffer pointer\n- nBytes (dword): Number of bytes to copy\n\nReturns:\n- Destination pointer (pdwDest) for chaining\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x7: Unroll threshold (copy at least 8 DWORDs before loop)\n- 0x3: Alignment mask (checking 4-byte boundary)\n- 0x4: DWORD size, used for shifting byte counts",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
