      "name": "LocaleMapStringWithConversion",
      "signature": "BOOL LocaleMapStringWithConversion(uint dwType, char * szSrc, int nSrcLen, ushort * pwDest, uint dwCodePage, uint dwLocale, int nFlags)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts a string to Unicode or ASCII based on locale settings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if string type mode is initialized; if not, detect via GetStringTypeW/A\n2. If Unicode mode (type 1), convert via MultiByteToWideChar and call GetStringTypeW\n3. If ANSI mode (type 2), call GetStringTypeA directly\n4. Return success/failure flag\n\nParameters:\n- dwType (uint): Character classification type (CT_*)\n- pszSrc (char *): Source string pointer\n- nSrcLen (int): Source string length in characters\n- pwDest (ushort *): Destination buffer for classification result\n- nCodePage (uint): Code page for conversion (0 = default)\n- nLocale (uint): Locale ID for classification (0 = default)\n- nFlags (int): Conversion flags (bit 0 = use flags bit 0)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 (TRUE) on success, 0 (FALSE) on failure\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- If nCodePage is 0, uses g_nDefaultCodePage\n- If nLocale is 0, uses g_dwStringCompareMode\n- Handles both Unicode and ANSI string modes transparently",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:a7046d73bbd286a50d5e7204509858d2",
