      "name": "GetStringLengthWithLimit",
      "signature": "int GetStringLengthWithLimit(char * szString, int nMaxLen)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Calculate the length of a string up to a maximum character limit.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize current pointer to string start and remaining count to max length\n2. Loop while remaining count > 0:\n   - Decrement remaining count\n   - Check if current character is null terminator; break if found\n   - Advance to next character\n3. If null terminator found at or before max length, return actual string length\n4. Otherwise, return max length (string exceeds limit)\n\nParameters:\n- szString (char*): String to measure\n- nMaxLen (int): Maximum characters to scan\n\nReturns:\n- Length of string if within limit, or nMaxLen if string exceeds limit",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
