      "name": "IsTimeInRange",
      "signature": "bool IsTimeInRange(int * pTimeValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Validates if a time value is within an allowed range.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if copy mode is enabled (g_fCopyEnabled)\n2. If disabled, return false immediately\n3. Extract time value from param[5] and validate against DAT_6f9221a8/DAT_6f9221b8\n4. If time is in restricted set, perform additional validation checks\n5. Extract hours from param[7] and compare against global time range bounds\n6. For times within bounds, calculate milliseconds via (hours * 60 + minutes) * 60 + seconds) * 1000\n7. Return true if value is in valid range, false otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- pTimeValue (int*): Pointer to time array [seconds, minutes, hours, ?, ?, value, ?, hours_check, ...]\n\nReturns:\n- true if time is within allowed range, false otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3c (60): Seconds/minutes per unit\n- 0x3e8 (1000): Milliseconds multiplier\n- DAT_6f9221ac/bc: Time range bounds",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
