      "name": "WriteBufferData",
      "signature": "int WriteBufferData(DWORD dwHandle, char * pbData, uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Writes data to file handle with text mode support (CRLF conversion).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If size is 0, return 0\n2. Check buffer's seek flag and update if needed\n3. If binary mode: direct WriteFile call\n4. If text mode: scan for LF, convert to CRLF, write in chunks\n5. Return bytes written or error code\n\nParameters:\n- dwHandle (DWORD): File handle ID (index into buffer table)\n- pbData (char*): Data to write\n- nSize (uint): Bytes to write\n\nReturns:\n- Bytes successfully written on success\n- 0 on failure or empty write\n- Negative on error\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x24 (36): Structure stride per handle entry\n- 0x20 (32): Seek flag mask (bit 5)\n- 0x80 (128): Binary mode flag (bit 7)\n- 0x40 (64): CRLF termination flag (bit 6)\n- 0x1a (26): EOF marker (Ctrl+Z) for text termination\n- 0x400 (1024): Buffer size for intermediate conversion",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
