      "name": "BufferIsProtected",
      "signature": "byte BufferIsProtected(uint dwBufferId)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Returns protection flag (0x40 bit) for buffer handle validation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate buffer handle is within limit (g_dwHandleLimit)\n2. If handle exceeds limit, return 0 (unprotected)\n3. Extract table index using high 27 bits of handle (handle >> 5)\n4. Get table entry from g_pBufferTable[index]\n5. Calculate offset using low 5 bits (handle & 0x1f) with stride 0x24\n6. Access flags field at table_entry + 4 + offset\n7. Extract and return 0x40 bit (protection flag)\n\nParameters:\n- dwBufferId (uint): Buffer handle to check\n\nReturns:\n- 0x40 if buffer is protected/locked, 0 if unprotected\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1f (31): Mask for low 5 bits (32 buffer slots per table entry)\n- 0x5: Right shift amount for high 27 bits\n- 0x24 (36): Stride/size of buffer record structure\n- 0x40 (64): Protection/locked flag bit value",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d020e6e6f383c625d5fd112b88b641eb",
