      "name": "IsBitfieldRangeEmpty",
      "signature": "int IsBitfieldRangeEmpty(uint dwBitfieldPtr, int nBitIndex)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Checks if a bitfield range from nBitIndex onwards contains only empty bits.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if the bit at nBitIndex in the target word is empty (0)\n2. If not empty, return 0 (range contains set bits)\n3. Otherwise, check all remaining words from word_index+1 to word 2 (inclusive)\n4. If any remaining word is non-zero, return 0\n5. If all bits in range are empty, return 1\n\nParameters:\n- dwBitfieldPtr (uint): Pointer to array of bitfield words (32-bit each)\n- nBitIndex (int): Starting bit index to check (0-63, logically 0-95 for 3 words)\n\nReturns:\n- 1 if all bits from nBitIndex onwards are empty (0)\n- 0 if any bit in range is set (1)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:546b5c43c0effce0a0403e1069ea2e2c",
