      "name": "BitRotateArray",
      "signature": "void BitRotateArray(uint * pdwArray, uint dwShift)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Rotates bits in an array of dwords by a specified number of positions.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Parse shift amount into word position (nShift / 32) and bit position (nShift % 32)\n2. For each of 3 dwords, rotate right by nBitPos bits with carry from next element\n3. For remaining array elements, either zero or copy from appropriate source based on word position\n\nParameters:\n- pdwArray (uint*): Pointer to 3-dword array to rotate\n- nShift (uint): Number of bits to rotate right\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x20 (32): Bits per dword, used for word/bit position calculation\n- 3: Fixed array size (3 dwords = 96 bits total)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
