      "name": "ProcessExponentMantissa",
      "signature": "uint ProcessExponentMantissa(ushort * pExponentData, uint * pdwOutputBuffer, int * pnExponentParams)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Processes floating-point exponent and mantissa data.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract exponent value at offset 5 from input array\n2. Calculate normalized exponent by subtracting 0x3fff\n3. If exponent is special -0x3fff value, validate all values are zero\n4. For normal exponents, copy array and clear specified bitfield range\n5. Apply bit rotation operations based on range comparisons\n6. Combine sign bit, rotated offset, and final exponent value\n7. Output result to specified buffer format (32-bit or 64-bit)\n\nParameters:\n- pExponentData (ushort*): Input array with exponent at offset 5\n- pdwOutputBuffer (uint*): Output buffer for processed values\n- pnExponentParams (int*): Config array with range/rotation/format params\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Special exponent -0x3fff with zero validation success\n- 1: Bit rotation applied, valid result returned\n- 2: Normal processing path, result assembled\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3fff (16383): Exponent normalization constant\n- 0x8000 (32768): Sign bit mask\n- 0x7fff (32767): Exponent magnitude mask",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:7af322ad22a8e231117c7fe6d2adf33c",
