      "name": "strchr_ReturnPrevious",
      "signature": "char * strchr_ReturnPrevious(int nUnused, char * pszCurrent)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "comment": "strchr_ReturnPrevious - Return pointer to previous byte position\n\nInternal helper for _strchr library function. This is an exit point\njumped to from the alignment phase loop when the target character is\nfound. Since EDX was incremented past the matching byte before the\ncomparison, this function returns EDX-1 to point to the actual match.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Compute EAX = pszCurrent - 1 (LEA EAX,[EDX + -0x1])\n2. Restore EBX from stack (caller saved it)\n3. Return pointer to matched character\n\nParameters:\n  nUnused (ECX) - Unused, remnant from __fastcall convention\n  pszCurrent (EDX) - Pointer one byte past the matched character\n\nReturns:\n  char* - Pointer to the matched character (pszCurrent - 1)\n\nClassification: Thunk/Helper - Internal exit point for _strchr\n\nCalled from: _strchr at 0x6f91912d (JZ when char found during alignment)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:3ecdb5e459e29b4117490dc114e98574",
