      "name": "FindAllocTableEntry",
      "signature": "uint * FindAllocTableEntry(void * pBlock)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Searches allocation table for entry containing given memory block.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Start at g_pAllocTable base\n2. Iterate through entries (0x14 bytes each)\n3. Compare (pBlock - entry->baseAddr) against 0x100000 (1MB)\n4. Return entry pointer if within range, NULL if not found\n\nParameters:\n- pBlock (void*): Memory block address to locate\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to allocation table entry if found, NULL otherwise\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14 (20): Allocation table entry stride\n- 0x100000 (1MB): Maximum offset from base address\n- 0xc (12): Offset to base address field in entry",
