      "name": "AllocatePoolBlock",
      "signature": "void * AllocatePoolBlock(dword dwRequestSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates a memory block from the segregated free list pool allocator.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Align requested size to 16-byte boundary: (dwRequestSize + 0x17) & 0xFFFFFFF0\n2. Calculate size class index from aligned size (shift right 4, subtract 1)\n3. Build bitmask for size class (bits 0-31 for small, 32-63 for large)\n4. Search allocation table entries for one with free blocks in the size class\n5. If no suitable entry found, create new allocation table entry via CreateAllocTableEntry\n6. Initialize pool bucket for the entry via InitializePoolBucket if needed\n7. Find first free block in the appropriate size class bucket\n8. Unlink block from free list, update bitmap counters\n9. Split block if remainder is large enough for separate size class\n10. Mark allocated block with size+1 header/footer for in-use detection\n11. Return pointer to usable memory (after 4-byte header)\n\nParameters:\n- dwRequestSize: Requested allocation size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- void*: Pointer to allocated memory, or NULL on failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x17 (23): Alignment adjustment (16-byte align + 8-byte header overhead - 1)\n- 0x10 (16): Alignment granularity\n- 0x14 (20): Allocation table entry stride (5 DWORDs)\n- 0x20 (32): Boundary between low/high bitmask halves\n- 0x3F (63): Maximum size class index\n- 0x81 (129): Bucket stride in DWORDs\n- 0x11 (17): Offset to low bitmap array\n- 0x31 (49): Offset to high bitmap array\n- 0x51 (81): Offset to bucket free list heads\n\nRelated Functions:\n- CreateAllocTableEntry (FUN_6f9198f5): Creates new allocation region\n- InitializePoolBucket (FUN_6f9199a6): Initializes free list for size class",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ff64648b3e6e32bc28a5e4bc8d984c1e",
