      "name": "CreateAllocTableEntry",
      "signature": "AllocTableEntry * CreateAllocTableEntry(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Creates a new allocation table entry with heap and virtual memory allocations.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if table is full (g_dwAllocCount == g_dwAllocCapacity)\n2. If full, grow table by 0x10 entries using HeapReAlloc\n3. Calculate entry pointer: base + count * 0x14\n4. Allocate 0x41c4 byte heap block (HEAP_ZERO_MEMORY flag 0x8)\n5. Allocate 1MB virtual memory (MEM_RESERVE 0x2000, PAGE_READWRITE 0x4)\n6. Initialize entry fields and increment count\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to new AllocTableEntry on success\n- NULL if any allocation fails (cleans up partial allocations)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x14 (20): Entry stride (5 dwords)\n- 0x41c4 (16836): Heap block size\n- 0x100000 (1MB): Virtual memory reservation size\n- 0x50 (80): Base table size (0x10 entries * 5 dwords)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b59a8a7d2c8fdcc2aac183f01f99a847",
