      "name": "InitializePoolBucket",
      "signature": "int InitializePoolBucket(PoolHeader * pPoolHeader)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Initializes a new pool bucket for memory allocation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate bucket index by counting leading zero bits\n2. Compute offset to bucket free list area\n3. Initialize 63 empty doubly-linked list heads\n4. Allocate 32KB via VirtualAlloc at computed address\n5. Divide into 4KB pages with free block headers\n6. Link blocks into free list\n7. Update bucket state flags\n\nParameters:\n- pPoolHeader (PoolHeader*): Pool header structure\n\nReturns:\n- Bucket index (0-31) on success\n- -1 on allocation failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x204: Bucket descriptor stride\n- 0x144: First bucket offset\n- 0x8000: 32KB bucket size\n- 0x3F: 63 size class lists\n- 0xFF0: Usable bytes per page",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
