      "signature": "int TryResizePoolBlock(uint * pPoolHeader, byte * pbBlock, int nNewSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Attempts to resize a memory block in-place within a pool allocator.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Align requested size to 16-byte boundary (add 0x17, mask 0xFFFFFFF0)\n2. Calculate region index from block offset (block - base >> 15)\n3. Read current block size from header at pbBlock-4\n4. If new size > current: check next block for coalescence\n   a. Verify next block is free (bit 0 = 0) and combined size fits\n   b. Unlink next block from free list, update bucket bitmaps\n   c. If remainder exists, insert into appropriate free list\n5. If new size < current: split block\n   a. Optionally coalesce with free next block\n   b. Insert freed portion into appropriate free list bucket\n6. Update block size tags at both ends of resized block\n\nParameters:\n- pPoolHeader (uint*): Pool header with bitmaps at [0],[1] and data at [4]\n- pbBlock (byte*): Memory block address to resize\n- nNewSize (int): Requested new size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- 1 on successful resize (in-place)\n- 0 if resize not possible (next block in use or combined size insufficient)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x17: Alignment adjustment for 16-byte boundary\n- 0xFFFFFFF0: 16-byte alignment mask\n- 0x3F (63): Maximum bucket index\n- 0x20 (32): Bucket threshold for bitmap split (low/high)\n- 0x204 (516): Free list stride per region\n- 0x144 (324): Base offset to free lists in pool data\n- 0x44 (68): Low bucket bitmap array offset\n- 0xC4 (196): High bucket bitmap array offset\n- 0x80000000: MSB for bitmap bit operations",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e4f799c77acab14c5b1bdda2181c2d46",
