      "name": "AllocateMemoryPool",
      "signature": "void * * AllocateMemoryPool(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Allocates and initializes a memory pool for the slab allocator.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Select pool control block (static at 0x6f922660 if g_nPoolMode=-1, else HeapAlloc 0x2020 bytes)\n2. Reserve 4MB virtual address space (MEM_RESERVE, PAGE_READWRITE)\n3. Commit first 64KB of reserved space (MEM_COMMIT)\n4. Initialize linked list pointers (doubly-linked pool list)\n5. Initialize 1024 size class entries (8 bytes each, 0x2000 total)\n6. Zero first 64KB and initialize 16 page headers (4KB stride)\n7. Return pool pointer or NULL on failure\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- void**: Pointer to pool control block, NULL on allocation failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2020: Pool control block size (8 list ptrs + 1024*8 size entries)\n- 0x400000 (4MB): Virtual address reservation size\n- 0x10000 (64KB): Initial commit size\n- 0x400 (1024): Number of size class entries\n- 0xf1 (241): Size class maximum value\n- 0x1000 (4KB): Page stride for header initialization",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
