      "name": "ReleaseUnusedPoolPages",
      "signature": "void ReleaseUnusedPoolPages(int nMaxPages)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Releases unused pool pages by decommitting virtual memory.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Walk pool node list starting from g_pStaticPoolTail\n2. For each node with valid virtual memory (not 0xFFFFFFFF)\n3. Scan page table entries from high to low offset\n4. If entry is 0xF0 (releasable), call VirtualFree with MEM_DECOMMIT\n5. Mark freed entry as 0xFFFFFFFF and decrement g_nReleasablePages\n6. Update first-free pointer if this entry is lower\n7. After freeing pages, check if node is completely empty\n8. If all 0x400 entries are 0xFFFFFFFF, free the entire node\n9. Continue to next node until nMaxPages exhausted\n\nParameters:\n- nMaxPages (int): Maximum number of pages to release\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xF0: Page status indicating releasable\n- 0xFFFFFFFF: Page status indicating freed/invalid\n- 0x1000: Page size (4KB)\n- 0x4000: MEM_DECOMMIT flag\n- 0x400: Max entries per pool node (1024)\n- 0x3FF000: Starting offset (1023 pages * 4KB)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:4356a93c484fa354f7841c9d1d714a19",
