      "name": "FindStaticPoolSlot",
      "signature": "int FindStaticPoolSlot(byte * pbPtr, void * * ppPoolHeader, uint * pdwPageBase)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Finds the static pool slot index for a given pointer.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Traverse circular linked list starting from g_pStaticPoolHead\n2. For each pool, check if pbPtr falls within [pPool+0x10, pPool+0x14] range\n3. Return 0 if not found in any pool\n4. Validate alignment: pbPtr must be 16-byte aligned (& 0xF == 0)\n5. Validate page offset: (pbPtr & 0xFFF) must be >= 0x100\n6. Calculate slot index = ((pbPtr - pageBase - 0x100) >> 4) + 8 + pageBase\n\nParameters:\n- pbPtr (byte*): Pointer to find in static pools\n- ppPoolHeader (void**): OUT - receives pool header pointer\n- pdwPageBase (uint*): OUT - receives page-aligned base address\n\nReturns:\n- Slot index combining page base + slot offset on success\n- 0 if pointer not found or invalid alignment\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x10, 0x14: Pool header offsets for range start/end pointers\n- 0xF: 16-byte alignment mask\n- 0x100 (256): Page header size reserved at start\n- 0xFFF, 0xFFFFF000: Page offset and page base masks",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:d9739637e22d71ed7283b5bc68a6c4ac",
