      "name": "ReturnPoolSlotToPage",
      "signature": "void ReturnPoolSlotToPage(int * pPoolNode, int nPoolAddress, byte * pbSlotBlocks)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Returns a pool slot to its containing page, updating page block counts.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Calculate page table entry from pool node and address offset\n2. Add slot's block count to page's free block counter\n3. Clear slot's block count (mark slot as returned)\n4. Set page status to 0xF1 (released)\n5. If page is fully free (0xF0 blocks), increment releasable page counter\n6. When 32 pages are releasable, trigger batch release of 16 pages\n\nParameters:\n- pPoolNode (int*): Pool node structure containing page table at offset 0x18\n- nPoolAddress (int): Address within pool to calculate page index\n- pbSlotBlocks (byte*): Pointer to slot's block count (cleared on return)\n\nReturns:\n- void\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x18: Offset to page table array in pool node\n- 0x10: Offset to base address in pool node\n- 0xC (12): Page size shift (4KB pages)\n- 0x8: Page table entry stride (8 bytes per entry)\n- 0xF0 (240): Max blocks per page (page fully free threshold)\n- 0xF1 (241): Page status indicating released\n- 0x20 (32): Releasable pages threshold to trigger batch release\n- 0x10 (16): Number of pages to release in batch",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:ab1eb8b21e2bded2678160ac668c3175",
