      "name": "AllocateFromPool",
      "signature": "void * AllocateFromPool(uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Allocates memory block of requested size from the memory pool system.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Search active pool list (g_pPoolListHead) for suitable free block\n2. For each pool, scan allocation table entries (8-byte pairs: size, limit)\n3. If block found via FUN_6f91a297, subdivide and return allocated block\n4. If no block in active pools, search static pool list (g_pStaticPoolHead)\n5. If static pool has free pages marked -1, commit with VirtualAlloc\n6. Initialize committed pages with memset and set up block headers\n7. If all pools exhausted, call AllocateMemoryPool to create new pool\n8. Update pool head pointer and allocation table on success\n\nParameters:\n- dwSize (uint): Requested allocation size in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- void*: Pointer to allocated memory block (offset 0x100 from header)\n- NULL: Allocation failed (no memory available)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1000: Page size and block table stride\n- 0x2018: End offset of upper allocation table in pool\n- 0x18: Start offset of lower allocation table\n- 0xF0: Initial free space in new block (240 bytes)\n- 0xF1: Block limit marker (241)\n- 0x100: Offset from block header to user data (256 bytes)\n- 0x10: Maximum pages to commit at once (16)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:de76025ed2839a23b964285c7e0d5701",
