      "name": "InvokeNewHandler",
      "signature": "bool InvokeNewHandler(uint dwSize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Invokes the registered new-handler callback when memory allocation fails.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if g_pfnNewHandlerCallback is registered (non-NULL)\n2. If registered, call the handler with the requested allocation size\n3. Return TRUE if handler succeeded (non-zero), FALSE otherwise\n\nParameters:\n- dwSize (uint): Size of the failed allocation request in bytes\n\nReturns:\n- TRUE (1) if handler succeeded and caller should retry allocation\n- FALSE (0) if no handler registered or handler failed\n\nRelated Functions:\n- __nh_malloc: Calls this on allocation failure\n- AllocateZeroedMemory: Calls this on allocation failure",
