      "name": "LocaleAwareAtoi",
      "signature": "int LocaleAwareAtoi(char * szStr)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts string to integer with locale-aware character classification (atoi equivalent).\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip leading whitespace using character transform table (flag 0x8 = isspace)\n2. Check for optional sign character ('+' 0x2b or '-' 0x2d)\n3. Convert consecutive digit characters to integer (flag 0x4 = isdigit)\n4. Apply sign negation if leading character was '-'\n\nParameters:\n- szStr (char*): Null-terminated input string\n\nReturns:\n- Parsed integer value (negated if preceded by minus sign)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x2b: ASCII '+' (plus sign)\n- 0x2d: ASCII '-' (minus sign)\n- 0x30: ASCII '0' (digit base for conversion)\n- 0x8: Character classification flag for whitespace (isspace)\n- 0x4: Character classification flag for digit (isdigit)\n\nRelated Functions:\n- TransformCharacterWithFlags: Used for locale-aware character classification",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:534e7e7fed8d48d41353dab6322de72f",
