      "name": "GetEnvironmentVariable",
      "signature": "char * GetEnvironmentVariable(char * szVarName)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Searches for an environment variable value in the command-line arguments array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if command-line arguments have been processed (g_fProcessed)\n2. If args array (g_ppCommandArgs) not initialized, attempt to initialize via FUN_6f91b6e7\n3. Iterate through args array looking for \"VARNAME=value\" pattern\n4. Use case-insensitive multibyte comparison (__mbsnbicoll) to match variable name\n5. Return pointer to value portion (after '=') if found\n\nParameters:\n- szVarName: Environment variable name to search for (e.g., \"TZ\")\n\nReturns:\n- Pointer to value string if found, NULL otherwise\n\nRelated Functions:\n- FUN_6f91b6e7: Initializes command args from wide-char environment\n- InitializeTimeZoneInfo: Primary caller, retrieves TZ variable",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
