      "name": "MapWinErrorToErrno",
      "signature": "void MapWinErrorToErrno(DWORD dwWinError)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Maps Windows error code to C runtime errno.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Store Windows error in TLS slot 3 (GetTlsWinErrorPtr)\n2. Search g_adWinToErrnoMap table for matching error code\n3. If found, store mapped errno in TLS slot 2 (GetTlsErrnoPtr)\n4. If not found, check special ranges:\n   - 0x13-0x24: ERROR_WRITE_PROTECT to ERROR_SHARING_BUFFER_EXCEEDED \u2192 EACCES (0xD)\n   - 0xBC-0xCA: ERROR_INVALID_ORDINAL to ERROR_INVALID_MODULETYPE \u2192 ENOEXEC (8)\n5. Default unmapped errors \u2192 EINVAL (0x16)\n\nParameters:\n- dwWinError (DWORD): Windows error code from GetLastError\n\nReturns:\n- void: Sets TLS errno value, no return\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0xD (13): EACCES - permission denied\n- 0x8: ENOEXEC - exec format error\n- 0x16 (22): EINVAL - invalid argument (default)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:1f1ea39570d78b40a761876432663560",
