      "name": "GetFileHandleFromBuffer",
      "signature": "HANDLE GetFileHandleFromBuffer(uint dwBufferId)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Retrieves a file handle from the internal buffer table.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate buffer ID is within the handle limit\n2. Calculate buffer entry location using 32-entry group indexing\n3. Check if buffer entry is valid (bit 0 set in state flags)\n4. If valid, return the stored file handle\n5. If invalid, set errno to 9 (EBADF) and clear Win32 error\n\nParameters:\n- dwBufferId (uint): Index into the buffer table\n\nReturns:\n- Valid file handle on success\n- 0xffffffff on failure (invalid buffer ID or inactive entry)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x1f (31): Mask for entry index within 32-entry group\n- 0x24 (36): Size of each buffer entry structure\n- 0x9: EBADF errno value (bad file descriptor)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:925a8d581e90d1850e90a2aaf94686cb",
