      "name": "FlushFileBuffer",
      "signature": "int FlushFileBuffer(int * pFileStruct)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Flushes pending write data from a file buffer to disk.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check if file is in write mode (flags & 3 == 2) and has data to flush (flags & 0x108)\n2. Calculate data size: current position - buffer base\n3. If positive data size, call BufferWriteData to write pending data\n4. On success: clear dirty flag (0xFD mask). On failure: set error flag (0x20), return -1\n5. Reset buffer: count = 0, current position = buffer base\n\nParameters:\n- pFileStruct (int*): File structure pointer with fields:\n  [0] current pointer, [1] count, [2] base pointer, [3] flags, [4] file handle\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success or no data to flush\n- -1 on write failure\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x108: Write pending flags mask\n- 0x80: Dirty/modified flag\n- 0x20: Error flag\n- 0xFD: Clear write mode mask",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:4c053343a65baac58fac65c0d3534b2b",
