      "name": "FlushAllBuffers",
      "signature": "int FlushAllBuffers(int nFlushMode)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Flushes all active file buffers in the buffer array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Acquire global critical section (index 2)\n2. Iterate through all buffers in g_pBufferArray\n3. For each buffer with valid flags (0x83 = active|open|modified):\n   - Acquire buffer-specific critical section\n   - If nFlushMode=1: Flush buffer, count successes\n   - If nFlushMode=0 and dirty (0x2): Flush buffer, set error on failure\n   - Release buffer critical section\n4. Release global critical section\n5. Return success count (mode 1) or error status (mode 0)\n\nParameters:\n- nFlushMode (int): 0=flush only dirty buffers (return -1 on failure),\n                    1=flush all active buffers (return count of successes)\n\nReturns:\n- Mode 1: Count of successfully flushed buffers\n- Mode 0: 0 on success, -1 if any flush failed\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x83: Buffer flags mask (active|open|modified)\n- 0x2: Dirty/modified flag",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:e7b052927c73f8415c227814d8219b82",
