      "name": "ConvertDigitsTo96BitFloat",
      "signature": "void ConvertDigitsTo96BitFloat(byte * pbDigits, int nDigitCount, uint * pdwMantissa)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts ASCII digit string to 96-bit extended precision float mantissa.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 96-bit accumulator to zero, exponent to 0x404E\n2. For each digit: multiply accumulator by 10 (shift*4 + original = *5, shift = *10)\n3. Add current digit value (0-9) to accumulator\n4. Normalize: shift left by 16 bits while high dword is zero\n5. Normalize: shift left by 1 bit while high bit not set\n6. Store final exponent at mantissa[10] (offset +0xA)\n\nParameters:\n- pbDigits (byte*): Array of digit values (NOT ASCII - already converted 0-9)\n- nDigitCount (int): Number of digits to process\n- pdwMantissa (uint*): Output 12-byte (96-bit) mantissa buffer\n\nReturns:\n- void (result stored in pdwMantissa)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x404E: Initial exponent bias for 80-bit float\n- 0xFFF0: Exponent adjustment per 16-bit shift (-16)\n- 0xFFFF: Exponent adjustment per 1-bit shift (-1)\n- 0x8000: High bit mask for normalization check",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
      "index": "MNE:b41de5b81e6f5c290111b6d697b33467",
