      "name": "ParseFloatString",
      "signature": "void ParseFloatString(void * this, void * pOutput, ushort * pResult, int * pnEndPtr, byte * pbInput, int nPrecision, int nDefaultExp, int nExpAdjust, int nAllowSign)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Parses a floating-point number string into internal representation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Skip leading whitespace (space, tab, newline, CR)\n2. Parse optional sign (+/-) and set wSign\n3. Collect digits before decimal point via state machine\n4. Handle decimal separator from g_byCharacterSwapValue\n5. Collect fractional digits after decimal\n6. Parse optional exponent (E/e with +/- and digits)\n7. Limit digits to 25 (0x19), track overflow count\n8. Convert digit buffer to mantissa via FUN_6f91ad42\n9. Apply exponent adjustments and precision scaling\n10. Call FUN_6f91ba85 to finalize float representation\n\nParameters:\n- pThis (void*): Context pointer (unused internally)\n- pResult (ushort*): 12-byte output buffer for float representation\n- pnEndPtr (int*): Receives pointer to first unparsed char\n- pbInput (byte*): Input string to parse\n- nPrecision (int): Precision control parameter\n- nDefaultExp (int): Default exponent when none specified\n- nExpAdjust (int): Exponent adjustment value\n- fAllowSign (int): If non-zero, allows +/- before exponent\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Success\n- 1: Underflow\n- 2: Overflow\n- 4: Invalid/empty input\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x19 (25): Maximum digits to collect\n- 0x1450 (5200): Maximum exponent magnitude\n- 0x8000: Negative sign flag\n- 0x30 ('0'): ASCII digit base",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
