      "name": "ConvertExtendedToDecimalString",
      "signature": "int ConvertExtendedToDecimalString(uint dwMantissaLo, uint dwMantissaHi, uint dwSignAndExp, int nPrecision, byte bFlags, short * pOutput)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Converts 80-bit extended precision float to decimal string.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Extract sign (0x8000) and biased exponent (0x7FFF mask)\n2. Set sign char: '-' for negative, ' ' for positive\n3. If mantissa/exponent all zero: output \"0\" and return 1\n4. If exponent == 0x7FFF (special): detect INF/NaN/IND\n5. Estimate decimal exponent via log10 approximation formula\n6. Normalize via FUN_6f91ba85 scaling by -decimalExp\n7. If exp >= 0x3FFF: increment decimalExp, divide by 10\n8. Extract digits via multiply-by-10 loop (max 21 digits)\n9. Round: if last digit > '4', propagate carry backward\n10. Strip trailing zeros, set string length, null-terminate\n\nParameters:\n- dwMantissaLo (uint): Low 32 bits of mantissa\n- dwMantissaHi (uint): High 32 bits of mantissa  \n- dwSignAndExp (uint): Sign bit 0x8000 + 15-bit exponent\n- nPrecision (int): Max decimal digits (clamped to 21)\n- bFlags (byte): Bit 0 = relative precision mode\n- pOutput (short*): Output buffer pointer\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Normal number converted successfully\n- 0: Special value (INF, NaN, IND) written to buffer\n\nOutput Buffer Layout (packed struct):\n- [0-1]: Decimal exponent (short)\n- [2]: Sign character '-' or ' '\n- [3]: Digit count (byte)\n- [4+]: ASCII digit chars (no decimal point)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:caf0293062c4e4caabf207f9f9a0ab4c",
