      "name": "CharToUpperLocale",
      "signature": "uint CharToUpperLocale(void * this, void * pContext, uint dwChar)",
      "calling_convention": "__thiscall",
      "comment": "Converts a character to uppercase using locale-aware rules.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. If g_dwStringCompareMode is 0, use ASCII-only:\n   - Convert 'a'-'z' (0x61-0x7a) to 'A'-'Z' by subtracting 0x20\n2. Otherwise, check if character is single-byte (< 0x100):\n   a. If g_dwCharacterTransformMode < 2, check transform table bit 2\n   b. Else call TransformCharacterWithFlags with flag 2\n   c. If character is not transformable, return unchanged\n3. Check high byte in transform table for DBCS lead byte (bit 0x80):\n   a. If not lead byte, use 1-byte conversion\n   b. If lead byte, swap bytes for 2-byte conversion\n4. Call LocaleMapStringWithConversion with LCMAP_UPPERCASE (0x200)\n5. Return converted character (1 or 2 bytes based on result length)\n\nParameters:\n- pContext (void*): Context pointer passed through to subroutines\n- dwChar (uint): Character code to convert (may be DBCS)\n\nReturns:\n- uint: Uppercase version of input character, or unchanged if not convertible\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x61 (97): ASCII 'a'\n- 0x7a (122): ASCII 'z'\n- 0x20 (32): ASCII case offset\n- 0x100 (256): Single-byte character boundary\n- 0x200: LCMAP_UPPERCASE flag\n- 0x80: DBCS lead byte indicator bit",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
