      "name": "ConvertWideEnvArgsToMultiByte",
      "signature": "int ConvertWideEnvArgsToMultiByte(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "comment": "Converts wide-character environment arguments array to multibyte strings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get pointer to wide-char env args from g_ppWideCharEnvArgs\n2. For each wide string in array (until NULL terminator):\n   a. Get required buffer size via WideCharToMultiByte (code page 1)\n   b. Allocate buffer with malloc\n   c. Convert wide string to multibyte\n   d. Pass converted string to FUN_6f91bd7e for environment processing\n3. Advance to next array element\n\nParameters:\n- None (void)\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success (all args converted)\n- 0xFFFFFFFF (-1) on failure (size calc, alloc, or conversion error)\n\nCalled by:\n- FUN_6f91bd7e: During environment variable setup\n- GetEnvironmentVariable: Environment initialization",
