      "name": "ScaleExtendedByPow10",
      "signature": "void ScaleExtendedByPow10(byte * pbExtended, int nExponent, int nInitialize)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Scales an 80-bit extended precision float by 10^nExponent.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Select positive (0x6f924898) or negative (0x6f9249f8) power-of-10 table\n2. Optionally zero first 2 bytes of result if nInitialize==0\n3. Process exponent in base-8 chunks (3 bits at a time)\n4. For each non-zero octal digit, multiply by precomputed 10^(digit*8^position)\n5. If table entry has high bit set, adjust exponent by -1 before multiply\n\nParameters:\n- pbExtended (byte*): 12-byte extended precision float (in/out)\n- nExponent (int): Power of 10 to scale by (can be negative)\n- nInitialize (int): If 0, zero first 2 bytes before scaling\n\nReturns:\n- void (result stored in pbExtended)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x6f924898: Positive powers of 10 table base\n- 0x6f9249f8: Negative powers of 10 table base\n- 0x54 (84): Table row stride (7 entries * 12 bytes)\n- 0xC (12): Entry size (80-bit extended float)\n- 0x7fff: Exponent overflow check mask",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
