      "name": "CompareStringsLocaleAware",
      "signature": "int CompareStringsLocaleAware(LCID dwLocale, DWORD dwFlags, byte * pbStr1, int nLen1, byte * pbStr2, int nLen2, UINT nCodePage)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Compares two strings using locale-aware collation.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Check global DAT_6f9cdf3c for API support (0=unknown, 1=Wide, 2=ANSI)\n2. If unknown, probe CompareStringW then CompareStringA to detect\n3. Get effective string lengths via GetStringLengthWithLimit\n4. If ANSI mode: call CompareStringA directly\n5. If Wide mode: convert both strings via MultiByteToWideChar, then CompareStringW\n6. Handle edge cases: zero-length strings, lead byte detection\n\nParameters:\n- dwLocale (LCID): Locale identifier for comparison\n- dwFlags (DWORD): Comparison flags (NORM_IGNORECASE, etc.)\n- pbStr1 (byte*): First string buffer\n- nLen1 (int): Length of first string (-1 for null-terminated)\n- pbStr2 (byte*): Second string buffer\n- nLen2 (int): Length of second string (-1 for null-terminated)\n- nCodePage (UINT): Code page for multi-byte conversion (0=default)\n\nReturns:\n- 0: Error occurred\n- 1: str1 < str2\n- 2: str1 == str2\n- 3: str1 > str2\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 9 (MB_COMPOSITE): MultiByteToWideChar flag for composite chars\n- 1: First MultiByteToWideChar pass uses MB_PRECOMPOSED",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "MNE",
