      "name": "SetEnvVarFromString",
      "signature": "int SetEnvVarFromString(char * szEnvStr, int nSetEnv)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Parses and sets an environment variable from \"NAME=VALUE\" string format.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Validate input string is non-null and contains '=' separator\n2. Check if value portion after '=' is empty (deletion case)\n3. Initialize global env table if null, converting wide args if needed\n4. Search for existing entry with matching name in table\n5. If not found or table empty, expand table and add entry\n6. If found and value empty, remove entry and compact table\n7. If found and value non-empty, update entry pointer\n8. If nSetEnv flag set, call SetEnvironmentVariableA to sync OS env\n\nParameters:\n- szEnvStr (char*): Environment string in \"NAME=VALUE\" format\n- nSetEnv (int): Flag to also set via Windows API (non-zero = set)\n\nReturns:\n- 0 on success\n- -1 (0xFFFFFFFF) on error (null input, no '=', malloc failure)\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x3D (61): ASCII '=' character delimiter",
