      "name": "FindEnvVarIndex",
      "signature": "int FindEnvVarIndex(char * szVarName, size_t nNameLen)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Searches for an environment variable name in the command arguments array.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Get pointer array from g_ppCommandArgs\n2. Loop through each string in the array\n3. Use __mbsnbicoll for case-insensitive comparison of first nNameLen bytes\n4. If match found and next char is '=' or '\\0', return positive index\n5. If not found, return negated index (count of entries checked)\n\nParameters:\n- szVarName: Variable name to search for\n- nNameLen: Length of variable name to compare\n\nReturns:\n- Positive index if variable found (index into g_ppCommandArgs array)\n- Negative count if not found (-number of entries checked)",
