      "name": "DuplicateStringArray",
      "signature": "char * * DuplicateStringArray(char * * ppszSourceArray)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "comment": "Creates a deep copy of a null-terminated array of strings.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Return NULL if input array is NULL\n2. Count strings by iterating until NULL terminator found\n3. Allocate new array with (count+1) pointers via malloc\n4. Exit with error code 9 if allocation fails\n5. Duplicate each string via DuplicateString (malloc+strcpy)\n6. Write NULL terminator to end of new array\n7. Return pointer to duplicated array\n\nParameters:\n- ppszSourceArray (char**): Null-terminated array of string pointers\n\nReturns:\n- char**: Newly allocated array with duplicated strings, NULL-terminated\n- NULL: If input was NULL\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x4: Size of each pointer (4 bytes on x86)\n- 9: CRT error code for insufficient memory (__amsg_exit)",
